const e="tiantiandu-1b",n="小马过河",a="The Little Horse Crosses the River",i="中文天天读",o="Reading China",t="1B",s=[{n:1,title:"小心地滑",py:"Xiǎoxīn dì huá",en:"Caution: Slippery Floor",chars:106,daodu:"商场里常常能看到“小心地滑”的牌子。这四个字你会读吗？杰克读了，可是好像读错了……",daoduEn:"You often see signs saying “小心地滑” in shopping malls. Can you read these four characters? Jack read them, but it seems he got them wrong…",paras:[{zh:"今天是星期天。杰克和他的中国朋友李小明去逛商场。杰克一进商场就开始滑着走。",py:"Jīntiān shì xīngqītiān. Jiékè hé tā de Zhōngguó péngyou Lǐ Xiǎomíng qù guàng shāngchǎng. Jiékè yí jìn shāngchǎng jiù kāishǐ huázhe zǒu.",en:"Today is Sunday. Jack and his Chinese friend Li Xiaoming went shopping at a mall. As soon as Jack walked into the mall, he started sliding along as he walked."},{zh:"一不小心，杰克滑倒了。",py:"Yí bù xiǎoxīn, Jiékè huádǎo le.",en:"Then, not being careful, Jack slipped and fell."},{zh:"小明觉得很奇怪，就问杰克：“你为什么滑着走呢？”",py:"Xiǎomíng juéde hěn qíguài, jiù wèn Jiékè: “Nǐ wèi shénme huázhe zǒu ne?”",en:'Xiaoming thought it was very strange, so he asked Jack, "Why are you sliding as you walk?"'},{zh:"杰克指着地上的牌子说：“这里写着‘小心地滑’，我非常小心，可还是滑倒了。”",py:"Jiékè zhǐzhe dì shang de páizi shuō: “Zhèlǐ xiězhe ‘xiǎoxīn de huá’, wǒ fēicháng xiǎoxīn, kě háishi huádǎo le.”",en:`Jack pointed at the sign on the floor and said, "It says here 'xiǎoxīn de huá' (slide carefully). I was very careful, but I still fell."`},{zh:"小明大笑：“是‘小心地滑’，不是‘小心地滑’。”",py:"Xiǎomíng dà xiào: “Shì ‘xiǎoxīn dì huá’, bú shì ‘xiǎoxīn de huá’.”",en:`Xiaoming laughed out loud: "It's 'xiǎoxīn dì huá', not 'xiǎoxīn de huá'!" (地 read "dì" means "floor", so the sign says "Careful, slippery floor". Read "de", it turns 小心 into "carefully", so it seems to say "slide carefully".)`}],vocab:[{w:"逛",py:"guàng",pos:"v.",en:"stroll"},{w:"商场",py:"shāngchǎng",pos:"n.",en:"market, shopping mall"},{w:"开始",py:"kāishǐ",pos:"v.",en:"start, begin"},{w:"滑",py:"huá",pos:"v.",en:"slide, slip"},{w:"奇怪",py:"qíguài",pos:"adj.",en:"strange, odd"},{w:"指",py:"zhǐ",pos:"v.",en:"point to"},{w:"牌子",py:"páizi",pos:"n.",en:"sign"},{w:"笑",py:"xiào",pos:"v.",en:"smile, laugh"}],points:[{name:"一不小心",en:"carelessly, by accident",eg:"一不小心，杰克滑倒了。",egEn:"Jack wasn’t careful and slipped and fell.",zh:"“一不小心”是一个常用的说法，意思是“没注意”“不留神”，后面常说出现了不好的结果，比如摔倒、打破东西等。",enx:"“一不小心” is a common expression meaning “not paying attention” or “by accident”. It is usually followed by something unpleasant that happened, such as falling down or breaking something.",egs:["（1）一不小心，我把杯子打破了。","（2）下雨天路很滑，一不小心就会摔倒。"]},{name:"觉得",en:"think",eg:"小明觉得很奇怪，就问杰克。",egEn:"Xiaoming found it strange, so he asked Jack.",zh:"“觉得”，动词，表示有某种感觉，或者对人和事有某种看法，后面可以跟形容词，也可以跟一个句子。",enx:"“觉得” is a verb meaning “to feel” or “to think”. It expresses a feeling or an opinion, and can be followed by an adjective or a clause.",egs:["（1）今天有点儿冷，我觉得不太舒服。","（2）你觉得这本书怎么样？"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"今天是星期六。",a:!1},{q:"杰克和李小明是同学。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"杰克滑倒了，是因为他（ ）。",options:["不小心","汉语不太好","汉语太好了"],answer:1},{q:"“小心地滑”的“地”读音是（ ）。",options:["dì","de","di"],answer:0}],tip:{title:"“和”字的五种读音",titleEn:"The Five Pronunciations of “和”",zh:"汉语里有不少多音字：一个字有几个读音，读音不同，意思也常常不同。“和”就是一个例子，它有五种读音：hé，比如“我和你”“和平”；hè，比如“一唱一和”；huó，比如“和面”；huò，比如“和稀泥”；hú，打麻将赢了的时候说“和了”。最常用的是hé。",en:"Chinese has many polyphonic characters: one character can have several pronunciations, and different pronunciations often mean different things. “和” is a good example. It has five readings: hé, as in “我和你” (you and me) and “和平” (peace); hè, as in “一唱一和” (one sings and the other echoes); huó, as in “和面” (to knead dough); huò, as in “和稀泥” (to smooth things over); and hú, which is said when you win at mahjong (“和了”). The most common reading is hé."}},{n:2,title:"“妈妈”的电话",py:"“Māma” de diànhuà",en:'A Call from "Mom"',chars:105,daodu:"小雪是个“成龙迷”。今天晚上成龙要来北京，可是那时候她要上课。她会想出什么办法呢？",daoduEn:"Xiaoxue is a big Jackie Chan fan. Tonight Jackie Chan is coming to Beijing, but she has class at that time. What idea will she come up with?",paras:[{zh:"小雪非常喜欢看成龙的电影，她是一个“成龙”迷。",py:"Xiǎoxuě fēicháng xǐhuan kàn Chéng Lóng de diànyǐng, tā shì yí gè “Chéng Lóng” mí.",en:"Xiaoxue loves watching Jackie Chan's films. She is a big Jackie Chan fan."},{zh:"今天晚上，成龙要来北京和影迷见面，小雪非常想去。但见面会是上课的时间。",py:"Jīntiān wǎnshang, Chéng Lóng yào lái Běijīng hé yǐngmí jiànmiàn, Xiǎoxuě fēicháng xiǎng qù. Dàn jiànmiànhuì shì shàngkè de shíjiān.",en:"This evening Jackie Chan is coming to Beijing to meet his fans, and Xiaoxue really wants to go. But the meet-and-greet is during class time."},{zh:"为了见到成龙，她想请假，不去上课了。",py:"Wèile jiàndào Chéng Lóng, tā xiǎng qǐngjià, bú qù shàngkè le.",en:"To see Jackie Chan, she wants to ask for time off and skip class."},{zh:"小雪想了想，就给老师打电话了：“老师，您好，小雪今天生病了，不能去上课了。”",py:"Xiǎoxuě xiǎngle xiǎng, jiù gěi lǎoshī dǎ diànhuà le: “Lǎoshī, nín hǎo, Xiǎoxuě jīntiān shēngbìng le, bù néng qù shàngkè le.”",en:`Xiaoxue thought for a moment, then phoned her teacher: "Hello, teacher. Xiaoxue is sick today and can't come to class."`},{zh:"老师问：“你是……？”",py:"Lǎoshī wèn: “Nǐ shì...?”",en:'The teacher asked, "And you are...?"'},{zh:"“我是我妈妈。”",py:"“Wǒ shì wǒ māma.”",en:`"I'm my mom."`}],vocab:[{w:"喜欢",py:"xǐhuan",pos:"v.",en:"like, love"},{w:"电影",py:"diànyǐng",pos:"n.",en:"movie"},{w:"见面会",py:"jiànmiànhuì",pos:"n.",en:"fan meeting"},{w:"为了",py:"wèile",pos:"prep.",en:"in order to"},{w:"请假",py:"qǐngjià",pos:"v.",en:"ask for leave"},{w:"生病",py:"shēngbìng",pos:"v.",en:"get sick"},{w:"能",py:"néng",pos:"v.",en:"can, be able to"}],points:[{name:"迷",en:"fan, enthusiast",eg:"小雪是一个“成龙迷”。",egEn:"Xiaoxue is a Jackie Chan fan.",zh:"“迷”，名词，放在别的词后面，指非常喜欢某个人或某种东西的人，比如“成龙迷”“足球迷”“电影迷”。",enx:"“迷” is a noun. Placed after another word, it means a person who is very fond of someone or something, e.g. “成龙迷” (Jackie Chan fan), “足球迷” (football fan), “电影迷” (film fan).",egs:["（1）我哥哥是个足球迷，每个周末都看足球比赛。","（2）她是个电影迷，常常一个人去看电影。"]},{name:"见面",en:"meet",eg:"成龙要来北京和影迷见面。",egEn:"Jackie Chan is coming to Beijing to meet his fans.",zh:"“见面”，动词，表示两个人或很多人互相见到。常说“和/跟……见面”，后面不能再带宾语，不能说“见面你”。",enx:"“见面” is a verb meaning “to meet (each other)”. It is usually used as “和/跟……见面” and cannot take an object directly, so we don’t say “见面你”.",egs:["（1）明天下午我要和朋友见面。","（2）我们好久没见面了，你最近怎么样？"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"小雪很喜欢成龙的电影。",a:!0},{q:"小雪妈妈给老师打电话请假。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"小雪给老师打电话，是因为她（ ）。",options:["生病了","想看电影","想参加成龙的见面会"],answer:2},{q:"小雪说“我是我妈妈”后，老师可能会说（ ）。",options:["小雪的妈妈，你好","你是小雪","好的"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"成龙",titleEn:"Jackie Chan",zh:"成龙是世界有名的功夫电影明星，原名陈港生，1954年出生在中国香港。他演过很多电影，比如《醉拳》《A计划》《警察故事》，后来又在美国拍了《尖峰时刻》等电影，在很多国家都很受欢迎。他的电影里有很多精彩的功夫，也很好笑。成龙还很热心做慈善，常常帮助有困难的人。",en:"Jackie Chan is a world-famous kung fu film star. His original name is Chan Kong-sang, and he was born in Hong Kong, China, in 1954. He has acted in many films, such as Drunken Master, Project A and Police Story, and later made films in the US such as Rush Hour. He is popular in many countries. His films are full of exciting kung fu and are also very funny. Jackie Chan is also devoted to charity and often helps people in need."}},{n:3,title:"教师节快乐",py:"Jiàoshījié kuàilè",en:"Happy Teachers' Day",chars:124,daodu:"9月10日是中国的教师节。这一天，学生会对老师说什么？老师又会怎么回答呢？",daoduEn:"September 10th is Teachers’ Day in China. What do students say to their teachers on this day? And how do the teachers reply?",paras:[{zh:"一张明信片",py:"Yì zhāng míngxìnpiàn",en:"A Postcard",fmt:"h"},{zh:"亲爱的老师：",py:"Qīn'ài de lǎoshī:",en:"Dear Teacher,",fmt:"salute"},{zh:"您好！",py:"Nín hǎo!",en:"Hello!"},{zh:"今天是9月10日，中国的教师节。谢谢您教我们汉语，教我们中文歌。祝您节日快乐！",py:"Jīntiān shì 9 yuè 10 rì, Zhōngguó de Jiàoshījié. Xièxie nín jiāo wǒmen Hànyǔ, jiāo wǒmen Zhōngwén gē. Zhù nín jiérì kuàilè!",en:"Today is September 10th, Teachers' Day in China. Thank you for teaching us Chinese and teaching us Chinese songs. Happy Teachers' Day!"},{zh:"您的学生：李美子",py:"Nín de xuésheng: Lǐ Měizǐ",en:"Your student, Li Meizi",fmt:"sign"},{zh:"2010年9月10日",py:"2010 nián 9 yuè 10 rì",en:"September 10, 2010",fmt:"sign"},{zh:"一封Email",py:"Yì fēng Email",en:"An Email",fmt:"h"},{zh:"发件人：王一山 <wangyishan@bfsu.edu.cn>",py:"Fājiànrén: Wáng Yīshān <wangyishan@bfsu.edu.cn>",en:"From: Wang Yishan <wangyishan@bfsu.edu.cn>",fmt:"table"},{zh:"收件人：美子 <meizi@126.com>",py:"Shōujiànrén: Měizǐ <meizi@126.com>",en:"To: Meizi <meizi@126.com>",fmt:"table"},{zh:"日期：2010年9月12日上午10:20",py:"Rìqī: 2010 nián 9 yuè 12 rì shàngwǔ 10:20",en:"Date: September 12, 2010, 10:20 a.m.",fmt:"table"},{zh:"主题：谢谢！",py:"Zhǔtí: Xièxie!",en:"Subject: Thank you!",fmt:"table"},{zh:"美子同学：",py:"Měizǐ tóngxué:",en:"Dear Meizi,",fmt:"salute"},{zh:"你好！",py:"Nǐ hǎo!",en:"Hello!"},{zh:"谢谢你寄来的明信片。老师很高兴教你汉语，教你中文歌，希望你在中国生活好，学习好。",py:"Xièxie nǐ jìlái de míngxìnpiàn. Lǎoshī hěn gāoxìng jiāo nǐ Hànyǔ, jiāo nǐ Zhōngwén gē, xīwàng nǐ zài Zhōngguó shēnghuó hǎo, xuéxí hǎo.",en:"Thank you for the postcard you sent. I'm very happy to teach you Chinese and Chinese songs. I hope you live well and study well in China."},{zh:"王一山",py:"Wáng Yīshān",en:"Wang Yishan",fmt:"sign"},{zh:"2010年9月12日",py:"2010 nián 9 yuè 12 rì",en:"September 12, 2010",fmt:"sign"}],vocab:[{w:"明信片",py:"míngxìnpiàn",pos:"n.",en:"postcard"},{w:"亲爱的",py:"qīn'ài de",pos:"adj.",en:"dear"},{w:"您",py:"nín",pos:"pron.",en:"you"},{w:"寄",py:"jì",pos:"v.",en:"mail"},{w:"教",py:"jiāo",pos:"v.",en:"teach"},{w:"歌",py:"gē",pos:"n.",en:"song"},{w:"节日",py:"jiérì",pos:"n.",en:"festival"},{w:"生活",py:"shēnghuó",pos:"v.",en:"live"}],points:[{name:"寄",en:"mail, deliver by post",eg:"谢谢你寄来的明信片。",egEn:"Thank you for the postcard you sent.",zh:"“寄”，动词，意思是通过邮局把信、明信片、东西等送给别人，常说“给……寄……”，后面也常加“来”“去”。",enx:"“寄” is a verb meaning “to send (letters, postcards, parcels, etc.) by post”. It is often used as “给……寄……”, or with “来/去” after it: “寄来” (send here), “寄去” (send there).",egs:["（1）我昨天给妈妈寄了一张明信片。","（2）这些书你要寄到哪儿？"]},{name:"希望",en:"hope, wish for",eg:"希望你在中国生活好、学习好。",egEn:"I hope you live well and study well in China.",zh:"“希望”，动词，表示心里很想让某种情况出现，后面常跟一个句子或动词短语。",enx:"“希望” is a verb meaning “to hope”. It expresses a wish that something will happen and is often followed by a clause or a verb phrase.",egs:["（1）我希望明天不下雨。","（2）妈妈希望我多吃水果。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"王一山给美子寄了一张明信片。",a:!1},{q:"9月10日是中国的教师节。",a:!0},{q:"王老师很高兴教美子中文歌。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"中国的教师节",titleEn:"Teachers’ Day in China",zh:"尊敬老师是中国人的传统。1985年，中国把每年的9月10日定为教师节。这时新学年刚刚开始，学生们常常给老师送一张贺卡、一束花，或者说一句“老师，您辛苦了！”，表示感谢。很多国家也有自己的教师节，不过日期不一样。",en:"Respecting teachers is a Chinese tradition. In 1985, China made September 10th of every year Teachers’ Day. The new school year has just begun at that time, and students often give their teachers a card or a bunch of flowers, or say “Thank you for your hard work, teacher!” to show their thanks. Many other countries also have a Teachers’ Day, but on different dates."}},{n:4,title:"我叫马西文",py:"Wǒ jiào Mǎ Xīwén",en:"My Name Is Ma Xiwen",chars:132,daodu:"第一次上课，同学们要介绍自己。如果是你，你会怎么介绍自己？听听这四位留学生是怎么说的。",daoduEn:"On the first day of class, the students introduce themselves. How would you introduce yourself? Let’s listen to these four international students.",paras:[{zh:"大家好！现在自我介绍一下，我的名字叫马西文，是美国人。我喜欢唱歌、游泳。到中国以后，也开始喜欢打乒乓球了。",py:"Dàjiā hǎo! Xiànzài zìwǒ jièshào yíxià, wǒ de míngzi jiào Mǎ Xīwén, shì Měiguórén. Wǒ xǐhuan chànggē, yóuyǒng. Dào Zhōngguó yǐhòu, yě kāishǐ xǐhuan dǎ pīngpāngqiú le.",en:"Hello, everyone! Let me introduce myself. My name is Ma Xiwen, and I'm American. I like singing and swimming. Since coming to China, I've also started to like playing ping-pong."},{zh:"你们好！我是日本人，我的名字叫西川，我最喜欢的运动是骑自行车。你们呢？",py:"Nǐmen hǎo! Wǒ shì Rìběnrén, wǒ de míngzi jiào Xīchuān, wǒ zuì xǐhuan de yùndòng shì qí zìxíngchē. Nǐmen ne?",en:"Hi, everyone! I'm Japanese, and my name is Nishikawa. My favorite sport is cycling. How about you?"},{zh:"同学们好！我叫李美子，是韩国人。我喜欢中国菜，以后我们可以一起吃饭。",py:"Tóngxuémen hǎo! Wǒ jiào Lǐ Měizǐ, shì Hánguórén. Wǒ xǐhuan Zhōngguó cài, yǐhòu wǒmen kěyǐ yìqǐ chīfàn.",en:"Hello, classmates! I'm Li Meizi, and I'm Korean. I like Chinese food. Let's eat together sometime."},{zh:"朋友们，我是玛丽，法国人。很高兴认识大家，希望我们很快成为好朋友。",py:"Péngyoumen, wǒ shì Mǎlì, Fǎguórén. Hěn gāoxìng rènshi dàjiā, xīwàng wǒmen hěn kuài chéngwéi hǎo péngyou.",en:"Friends, I'm Marie, from France. I'm very glad to meet you all. I hope we'll soon become good friends."}],vocab:[{w:"大家",py:"dàjiā",pos:"pron.",en:"everybody"},{w:"自我介绍",py:"zìwǒ jièshào",pos:"v.",en:"introduce oneself"},{w:"唱歌",py:"chànggē",pos:"v.",en:"sing"},{w:"游泳",py:"yóuyǒng",pos:"v.",en:"swim"},{w:"乒乓球",py:"pīngpāngqiú",pos:"n.",en:"table tennis"},{w:"运动",py:"yùndòng",pos:"n.",en:"sports"},{w:"骑",py:"qí",pos:"v.",en:"ride"},{w:"自行车",py:"zìxíngchē",pos:"n.",en:"bicycle"},{w:"成为",py:"chéngwéi",pos:"v.",en:"become"}],points:[{name:"介绍",en:"introduce",eg:"现在自我介绍一下，我的名字叫马西文。",egEn:"Now let me introduce myself. My name is Ma Xiwen.",zh:"“介绍”，动词，意思是让别人知道一个人或一件事情，常说“介绍一下”“自我介绍”“给……介绍……”。",enx:"“介绍” is a verb meaning “to introduce”, i.e. to let others know about a person or a thing. Common patterns are “介绍一下”, “自我介绍” (introduce oneself) and “给……介绍……”.",egs:["（1）我给你们介绍一下，这是我的同学玛丽。","（2）你能给我介绍一个好饭馆吗？"]},{name:"认识",en:"know",eg:"很高兴认识大家，希望我们很快成为好朋友。",egEn:"I’m very glad to meet you all. I hope we’ll soon become good friends.",zh:"“认识”，动词，表示以前见过、知道某个人，也可以表示能认出某个字、某条路等。“很高兴认识你”是第一次见面时常说的话。",enx:"“认识” is a verb meaning “to know (someone)” or “to recognize (a character, a road, etc.)”. “很高兴认识你” (Nice to meet you) is often said when meeting someone for the first time.",egs:["（1）这个字你认识吗？","（2）我和他是在中国认识的。"]}],think:[],tf:[],mc:[],tip:{title:"哪些国家使用过汉字？",titleEn:"In Which Countries Were Chinese Characters Used?",zh:"汉字是中国人创造的，历史上也传到了中国周边的一些国家。日本、朝鲜半岛和越南都使用过汉字。今天，日语里还在用汉字，日本的常用汉字有两千多个；韩国和朝鲜现在主要用自己的文字，越南现在用拉丁字母。不过，在这些国家的语言里，还有很多词来自汉语。",en:"Chinese characters were created by the Chinese, and in history they also spread to some of China’s neighbouring countries. Japan, the Korean Peninsula and Vietnam all once used Chinese characters. Today Japanese still uses them, with over two thousand characters in common use. South Korea and North Korea now mainly use their own script, and Vietnam now uses the Latin alphabet. Even so, the languages of these countries still contain many words borrowed from Chinese."}},{n:5,title:"我是ABC",py:"Wǒ shì ABC",en:`I'm an "ABC"`,chars:128,daodu:"“ABC”是什么意思？“我”的妈妈是中国人，“我”为什么非常想早点儿去上海呢？",daoduEn:"What does “ABC” mean? The writer’s mother is Chinese. Why does the writer want so much to go to Shanghai soon?",paras:[{zh:"我爸爸是美国人，妈妈是中国人，大家都说我是ABC（American Born Chinese）。妈妈的老家在上海，外公和外婆现在还住在上海。",py:"Wǒ bàba shì Měiguórén, māma shì Zhōngguórén, dàjiā dōu shuō wǒ shì ABC (American Born Chinese). Māma de lǎojiā zài Shànghǎi, wàigōng hé wàipó xiànzài hái zhù zài Shànghǎi.",en:"My dad is American and my mom is Chinese, so everyone says I'm an ABC (American Born Chinese). My mom's hometown is Shanghai, and my grandpa and grandma (her parents) still live there."},{zh:"我小时候跟爸爸妈妈一起去过上海，但那是十年以前的事情了。",py:"Wǒ xiǎo shíhou gēn bàba māma yìqǐ qùguo Shànghǎi, dàn nà shì shí nián yǐqián de shìqing le.",en:"When I was little, I went to Shanghai with my mom and dad, but that was ten years ago."},{zh:"学校很快就放暑假了，我非常想早点儿去上海。为什么呢？因为我很喜欢外婆做的中国菜，还有今年的世博会在上海举行，那里一定非常有意思。",py:"Xuéxiào hěn kuài jiù fàng shǔjià le, wǒ fēicháng xiǎng zǎo diǎnr qù Shànghǎi. Wèi shénme ne? Yīnwèi wǒ hěn xǐhuan wàipó zuò de Zhōngguó cài, hái yǒu jīnnián de Shìbóhuì zài Shànghǎi jǔxíng, nàlǐ yídìng fēicháng yǒu yìsi.",en:"School will soon be out for the summer, and I really want to go to Shanghai as early as I can. Why? Because I love the Chinese food my grandma makes, and this year's World Expo is being held in Shanghai. It must be really interesting there."},{zh:"你不想去吗？",py:"Nǐ bù xiǎng qù ma?",en:"Don't you want to go?"}],vocab:[{w:"老家",py:"lǎojiā",pos:"n.",en:"hometown"},{w:"外公",py:"wàigōng",pos:"n.",en:"maternal grandfather"},{w:"外婆",py:"wàipó",pos:"n.",en:"maternal grandmother"},{w:"以前",py:"yǐqián",pos:"n.",en:"ago, earlier times"},{w:"暑假",py:"shǔjià",pos:"n.",en:"summer holiday"},{w:"住",py:"zhù",pos:"v.",en:"live"},{w:"菜",py:"cài",pos:"n.",en:"cuisine"},{w:"世博会",py:"shìbóhuì",pos:"n.",en:"World Expo"},{w:"一定",py:"yídìng",pos:"adv.",en:"surely"}],points:[{name:"举行",en:"hold, have",eg:"今年的世博会在上海举行。",egEn:"This year’s World Expo is being held in Shanghai.",zh:"“举行”，动词，意思是开展会议、比赛、活动等，后面常跟“会”“比赛”“活动”等词，也常说“……在……举行”。",enx:"“举行” is a verb meaning “to hold (a meeting, a match, an event, etc.)”. Its object is usually a word like “会”, “比赛” or “活动”. It is also often used as “……在……举行” (… is held in …).",egs:["（1）明天我们学校举行篮球比赛。","（2）这次见面会在北京饭店举行。"]},{name:"还有",en:"also, too, in addition",eg:"我很喜欢中国菜，还有今年的世博会在上海举行。",egEn:"I really like Chinese food; besides, this year’s World Expo is being held in Shanghai.",zh:"“还有”用来补充，表示除了前面说的以外，另外还有别的，常放在后一部分的开头。",enx:"“还有” is used to add more information, meaning “in addition, also”. It usually comes at the beginning of the added part.",egs:["（1）我想买苹果、香蕉，还有一些牛奶。","（2）今天的作业很多，还有，明天要考试。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"我没去过上海。",a:!1},{q:"今年的世博会在上海举行。",a:!0},{q:"我放暑假以后就去上海。",a:!0},{q:"我喜欢外婆做的中国菜。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"上海世博会",titleEn:"World Expo 2010 Shanghai China",zh:"2010年世界博览会在上海举行，时间是5月1日到10月31日，这是中国第一次举办综合类世博会。上海世博会的主题是“城市，让生活更美好”。它的会徽是用汉字“世”设计的，看起来像三个人手拉手。半年里，一共有七千多万人次参观了上海世博会。",en:"The 2010 World Expo was held in Shanghai from May 1st to October 31st — the first registered (general) World Expo ever hosted by China. Its theme was “Better City, Better Life”. The Expo emblem was designed from the Chinese character “世” (world) and looks like three people holding hands. In those six months, over 70 million visits were made to the Shanghai Expo."}},{n:6,title:"美人？没人？",py:"Měirén? Méi rén?",en:"Beauty? Nobody?",chars:130,daodu:"芳芳收到一条短信，非常高兴。她等了一整天，可是小乐一直没来。这是怎么回事呢？",daoduEn:"Fangfang got a text message and was very happy. She waited all day, but Xiaole never came. What happened?",paras:[{zh:"芳芳很喜欢张小乐，可是小乐不知道。一天早上，芳芳起床以后，看见一条短信：9点去找你，美人。小乐。",py:"Fāngfāng hěn xǐhuan Zhāng Xiǎolè, kěshì Xiǎolè bù zhīdào. Yì tiān zǎoshang, Fāngfāng qǐchuáng yǐhòu, kànjiàn yì tiáo duǎnxìn: 9 diǎn qù zhǎo nǐ, měirén. Xiǎolè.",en:`Fangfang really likes Zhang Xiaole, but Xiaole doesn't know. One morning, after getting up, Fangfang saw a text message: "Coming to see you at 9, beautiful. Xiaole."`},{zh:"芳芳非常高兴！",py:"Fāngfāng fēicháng gāoxìng!",en:"Fangfang was very happy!"},{zh:"这天，芳芳没有出去，从早上等到下午，可是小乐却没来。",py:"Zhè tiān, Fāngfāng méiyǒu chūqù, cóng zǎoshang děngdào xiàwǔ, kěshì Xiǎolè què méi lái.",en:"That day Fangfang didn't go out. She waited from morning till afternoon, but Xiaole never came."},{zh:"芳芳很生气，她给小乐打电话：“你为什么没来找我？”",py:"Fāngfāng hěn shēngqì, tā gěi Xiǎolè dǎ diànhuà: “Nǐ wèi shénme méi lái zhǎo wǒ?”",en:`Fangfang was very angry. She called Xiaole: "Why didn't you come to see me?"`},{zh:"小乐说：“我昨天晚上9点去找你了，你家没人啊！”",py:"Xiǎolè shuō: “Wǒ zuótiān wǎnshang 9 diǎn qù zhǎo nǐ le, nǐ jiā méi rén a!”",en:'Xiaole said, "I went to see you at 9 last night, but nobody was home!"'},{zh:"芳芳给小乐看了一下手机，原来昨天小乐把“没人”写成了“美人”。",py:"Fāngfāng gěi Xiǎolè kànle yíxià shǒujī, yuánlái zuótiān Xiǎolè bǎ “méi rén” xiěchéngle “měirén”.",en:'Fangfang showed Xiaole her phone. It turned out that the day before, Xiaole had typed "měirén" (美人, "beautiful") instead of "méi rén" (没人, "nobody") — they sound almost the same.'}],vocab:[{w:"起床",py:"qǐchuáng",pos:"v.",en:"get up"},{w:"短信",py:"duǎnxìn",pos:"n.",en:"text message"},{w:"从",py:"cóng",pos:"prep.",en:"from"},{w:"早上",py:"zǎoshang",pos:"n.",en:"morning"},{w:"等",py:"děng",pos:"v.",en:"wait"},{w:"生气",py:"shēngqì",pos:"v.",en:"get mad"},{w:"原来",py:"yuánlái",pos:"adv.",en:"it turns out that"}],points:[{name:"以后",en:"afterwards, later",eg:"芳芳起床以后，看见一条短信。",egEn:"After Fangfang got up, she saw a text message.",zh:"“以后”，名词，放在动词短语或时间词后面，表示在那个时间或那件事情的后面，比如“起床以后”“三个月以后”。",enx:"“以后” is a noun. Placed after a verb phrase or a time word, it means “after (that time or event)”, e.g. “起床以后” (after getting up), “三个月以后” (three months later).",egs:["（1）下课以后，我们去打篮球吧。","（2）吃饭以后不要马上睡觉。"]},{name:"V.+成",en:"verb + 成",eg:"原来昨天小乐把“没人”写成了“美人”。",egEn:"It turned out that yesterday Xiaole had typed “没人” (nobody) as “美人” (beauty).",zh:"“V.+成”中，“成”放在动词后面，表示动作让一个东西变成了另一个东西，常和“把”一起用：“把A V.成B”，比如“写成”“看成”“听成”。",enx:"In “V.+成”, “成” follows a verb to show that the action turns one thing into another. It is often used with “把”: “把A V.成B”, e.g. “写成” (write as), “看成” (mistake … for), “听成” (hear as).",egs:["（1）他把“大”字写成了“太”字。","（2）我把“四”听成了“十”。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"张小乐真喜欢芳芳。",a:!1},{q:"张小乐昨天去找芳芳了。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"小乐昨天晚上（ ）去找芳芳了。",options:["7点","8点","9点"],answer:2},{q:"芳芳为什么生气？（ ）",options:["小乐不喜欢她","小乐没给她打电话","小乐今天没来找她"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"姓名叠音",titleEn:"Reiterative Words in Names",zh:"中国人除了大名，常常还有小名，就是家里人叫的名字。小名常常用叠音，就是把一个字说两遍，比如“田田”“圆圆”“飞飞”“丽丽”，听起来很亲切、很可爱。不少人的大名也用叠音。本书故事里的“芳芳”“乐乐”“明明”，都是叠音名字。",en:"Besides their formal names, Chinese people often have a pet name used by their family. Pet names are often reduplicated — one character said twice — such as “田田”, “圆圆”, “飞飞” and “丽丽”, which sound warm and cute. Quite a few people’s formal names are reduplicated too. In the stories in this book, “芳芳”, “乐乐” and “明明” are all reduplicated names."}},{n:7,title:"怎么回家",py:"Zěnme huíjiā",en:"How Do I Get Home?",chars:109,daodu:"一个胖子想减肥，医生给了他一个好办法。三个月以后，他真的不胖了，可是又有了一个新问题……",daoduEn:"A fat man wanted to lose weight, and the doctor gave him a good idea. Three months later he really wasn’t fat any more, but now he had a new problem…",paras:[{zh:"一个胖子去看医生，问有什么好办法可以减肥。",py:"Yí gè pàngzi qù kàn yīshēng, wèn yǒu shénme hǎo bànfǎ kěyǐ jiǎnféi.",en:"A fat man went to see a doctor and asked if there was a good way to lose weight."},{zh:"医生说：“多吃蔬菜和水果，每天吃完饭以后走5公里。三个月以后再给我打电话。”",py:"Yīshēng shuō: “Duō chī shūcài hé shuǐguǒ, měi tiān chīwán fàn yǐhòu zǒu 5 gōnglǐ. Sān gè yuè yǐhòu zài gěi wǒ dǎ diànhuà.”",en:'The doctor said, "Eat lots of vegetables and fruit, and walk 5 kilometers after every meal. Call me again in three months."'},{zh:"三个月以后，这个胖子给医生打电话：“告诉您一个好消息！我已经不胖了。”",py:"Sān gè yuè yǐhòu, zhège pàngzi gěi yīshēng dǎ diànhuà: “Gàosu nín yí gè hǎo xiāoxi! Wǒ yǐjīng bú pàng le.”",en:`Three months later, the man called the doctor: "I have good news for you! I'm not fat anymore."`},{zh:"医生很高兴，说：“太好了！”",py:"Yīshēng hěn gāoxìng, shuō: “Tài hǎo le!”",en:'The doctor was very pleased and said, "Great!"'},{zh:"胖子接着说：“可是我现在在500公里以外，我怎么回家呢？”",py:"Pàngzi jiēzhe shuō: “Kěshì wǒ xiànzài zài 500 gōnglǐ yǐwài, wǒ zěnme huíjiā ne?”",en:`The man went on, "But now I'm 500 kilometers away. How do I get home?"`}],vocab:[{w:"胖子",py:"pàngzi",pos:"n.",en:"fat person"},{w:"医生",py:"yīshēng",pos:"n.",en:"doctor"},{w:"减肥",py:"jiǎnféi",pos:"v.",en:"lose weight"},{w:"蔬菜",py:"shūcài",pos:"n.",en:"vegetable"},{w:"水果",py:"shuǐguǒ",pos:"n.",en:"fruit"},{w:"告诉",py:"gàosu",pos:"v.",en:"tell"},{w:"消息",py:"xiāoxi",pos:"n.",en:"news"},{w:"已经",py:"yǐjīng",pos:"adv.",en:"already"},{w:"接着",py:"jiēzhe",pos:"adv.",en:"go on"}],points:[{name:"怎么",en:"how",eg:"我怎么回家呢？",egEn:"How am I going to get home?",zh:"“怎么”，代词，放在动词前面，用来问做事的方法，意思是“用什么办法”；也可以问原因，意思是“为什么”。",enx:"“怎么” is a pronoun. Placed before a verb, it asks about the way of doing something (“how”). It can also ask about the reason (“why, how come”).",egs:["（1）请问，去火车站怎么走？","（2）你怎么又来晚了？"]},{name:"以外",en:"beyond, outside, other than",eg:"我现在在500公里以外。",egEn:"I’m now 500 kilometers away.",zh:"“以外”，名词，放在数量词或表示地方的词后面，表示在某个范围的外边，和“以内”意思相反。",enx:"“以外” is a noun. Placed after a number phrase or a place word, it means “outside, beyond (a certain range)”. Its opposite is “以内” (within).",egs:["（1）他家在学校两公里以外。","（2）在一百米以外，我就看见他了。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"医生让胖子每天运动。",a:!1},{q:"胖子现在不胖了。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"胖子是怎么减肥的？他每天（ ）。",options:["不吃东西","多吃蔬菜、水果，走5公里","走500公里"],answer:1},{q:"医生让胖子（ ）以后给他打电话。",options:["一个月","三个月","五个月"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"中国传统的计量单位",titleEn:"Traditional Chinese Units of Measurement",zh:"中国有一些传统的计量单位，比如“斤”“两”“里”。今天的一斤是500克，一两是50克，十两是一斤；一里是500米，所以一公里就是两里。现在，在中国买菜、买水果的时候，人们还常常说“一斤苹果”“二两饺子”；说路的远近时，也常常说“几里路”。",en:"China has some traditional units of measurement, such as jin (斤), liang (两) and li (里). Today one jin is 500 grams, one liang is 50 grams, and ten liang make one jin; one li is 500 meters, so one kilometer is two li. In China today, people still often say “a jin of apples” or “two liang of dumplings” when buying food, and “a few li” when talking about distances."}},{n:8,title:"果然",py:"Guǒrán",en:"Sure Enough",chars:132,daodu:"老师让清水用“果然”这个词造句，清水说：“先吃水果，然后再……”他说对了吗？",daoduEn:"The teacher asked Shimizu to make a sentence with the word “果然”. He said, “First eat some fruit (水果), then (然后)…” Did he get it right?",paras:[{zh:"清水是日本人，他在中国留学已经两个多月了。他学习很努力，成绩也很好，但有时候他很调皮。",py:"Qīngshuǐ shì Rìběnrén, tā zài Zhōngguó liúxué yǐjīng liǎng gè duō yuè le. Tā xuéxí hěn nǔlì, chéngjì yě hěn hǎo, dàn yǒu shíhou tā hěn tiáopí.",en:"Shimizu is Japanese. He has been studying in China for over two months. He studies hard and gets good grades, but sometimes he's very cheeky."},{zh:"一个星期二的下午，清水正在上汉语课，学习“果然”这个词。",py:"Yí gè xīngqī'èr de xiàwǔ, Qīngshuǐ zhèngzài shàng Hànyǔ kè, xuéxí “guǒrán” zhège cí.",en:'One Tuesday afternoon, Shimizu was in Chinese class, learning the word "guǒrán" (果然, "sure enough").'},{zh:"老师说：“清水，请你用‘果然’这个词造句。”",py:"Lǎoshī shuō: “Qīngshuǐ, qǐng nǐ yòng ‘guǒrán’ zhège cí zàojù.”",en:`The teacher said, "Shimizu, please make a sentence with the word 'guǒrán'."`},{zh:"清水说：“先吃水果，然后再……”",py:"Qīngshuǐ shuō: “Xiān chī shuǐguǒ, ránhòu zài...”",en:'Shimizu said, "First eat some shuǐguǒ (水果, fruit), ránhòu (然后, then)..."'},{zh:"老师说：“不对，不对，‘果’和‘然’两个字不能分开！”",py:"Lǎoshī shuō: “Bú duì, bú duì, ‘guǒ’ hé ‘rán’ liǎng gè zì bù néng fēnkāi!”",en:`The teacher said, "No, no! You can't split the two characters 果 and 然!"`},{zh:"清水说：“老师，别着急，我还没说完呢。先吃水果，然后再喝可乐，果然很舒服。”",py:"Qīngshuǐ shuō: “Lǎoshī, bié zháojí, wǒ hái méi shuōwán ne. Xiān chī shuǐguǒ, ránhòu zài hē kělè, guǒrán hěn shūfu.”",en:`Shimizu said, "Don't worry, teacher, I haven't finished yet. First eat some fruit, then drink some cola, and sure enough (guǒrán), you feel great."`}],vocab:[{w:"努力",py:"nǔlì",pos:"adj.",en:"hard-working"},{w:"成绩",py:"chéngjì",pos:"n.",en:"academic record"},{w:"调皮",py:"tiáopí",pos:"adj.",en:"naughty"},{w:"用",py:"yòng",pos:"v.",en:"use"},{w:"先",py:"xiān",pos:"adv.",en:"first"},{w:"然后",py:"ránhòu",pos:"conj.",en:"then"},{w:"着急",py:"zháojí",pos:"adj.",en:"worried"},{w:"舒服",py:"shūfu",pos:"adj.",en:"comfortable"}],points:[{name:"分开",en:"separate, apart",eg:"‘果’和‘然’两个字不能分开！",egEn:"The two characters 果 and 然 can’t be separated!",zh:"“分开”，动词，意思是让在一起的人或东西不在一起，也可以表示人和人离开。",enx:"“分开” is a verb meaning “to separate”, i.e. to make people or things that are together no longer together. It can also mean that people part from each other.",egs:["（1）请把红的和白的分开放。","（2）我们是好朋友，从小到大没分开过。"]},{name:"果然",en:"sure enough",eg:"先吃水果，然后再喝可乐，果然很舒服。",egEn:"First eat some fruit, then drink some cola — sure enough, it feels great.",zh:"“果然”，副词，表示事情真的和以前说的或想的一样，常放在动词或形容词前面。",enx:"“果然” is an adverb meaning “sure enough, as expected”. It shows that what happened is just what was said or expected. It usually goes before a verb or an adjective.",egs:["（1）天气预报说今天下雨，果然下雨了。","（2）大家都说这个饭馆的菜好吃，我去吃了，果然很好吃。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"清水在日本留学两个月了。",a:!1},{q:"清水不会用“果然”造句。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"老师（ ），很着急。",options:["不喜欢清水","觉得清水说错了","生气了"],answer:1},{q:"清水学习很努力，（ ）成绩很好，但是有时候也很调皮。",options:["因为","所以","但是"],answer:1},{q:"清水学习很努力，所以成绩很好，（ ）有时候也很调皮。",options:["因为","所以","但是"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"汉语的字和词",titleEn:"Characters and Words in the Chinese Language",zh:"汉语的“字”和“词”不完全一样。字是一个一个的汉字；词是有意思、能单独用的语言单位。有的字自己就是一个词，比如“水”“吃”“好”；有的字要和别的字在一起才是词，比如“果”和“然”在一起是“果然”，意思和“水果”的“果”没有关系。现代汉语里，两个字的词最多。",en:"In Chinese, a “character” (字) and a “word” (词) are not exactly the same. A character is a single written unit; a word is a unit of language that has meaning and can be used on its own. Some characters are words by themselves, like “水” (water), “吃” (eat) and “好” (good). Others only form a word together with another character: “果” and “然” together make “果然” (sure enough), which has nothing to do with the “果” in “水果” (fruit). In modern Chinese, most words have two characters."}},{n:9,title:"方向错了",py:"Fāngxiàng cuò le",en:"The Wrong Direction",chars:127,daodu:"王明明去杭州旅行，钱快花完了。为了少花一元钱，他想了一个办法。这个办法好不好呢？",daoduEn:"Wang Mingming went on a trip to Hangzhou and had almost run out of money. To save one yuan, he came up with a plan. Was it a good plan?",paras:[{zh:"去年暑假，王明明去杭州旅行。杭州很漂亮，他去了很多地方，花了不少钱。",py:"Qùnián shǔjià, Wáng Míngmíng qù Hángzhōu lǚxíng. Hángzhōu hěn piàoliang, tā qùle hěn duō dìfang, huāle bù shǎo qián.",en:"Last summer vacation, Wang Mingming traveled to Hangzhou. Hangzhou is beautiful. He went to lots of places and spent quite a lot of money."},{zh:"有一天，他身上只有三元钱了。",py:"Yǒu yì tiān, tā shēnshang zhǐ yǒu sān yuán qián le.",en:"One day he had only three yuan left on him."},{zh:"他在公共汽车站问售票员：“从这里到西湖多少钱？”售票员回答：“四元。”他想：“我只有三元钱了，自己跑一会儿再坐车吧。”",py:"Tā zài gōnggòng qìchē zhàn wèn shòupiàoyuán: “Cóng zhèlǐ dào Xīhú duōshao qián?” Shòupiàoyuán huídá: “Sì yuán.” Tā xiǎng: “Wǒ zhǐ yǒu sān yuán qián le, zìjǐ pǎo yíhuìr zài zuò chē ba.”",en:`At the bus stop he asked the conductor, "How much is it from here to West Lake?" The conductor answered, "Four yuan." He thought, "I only have three yuan. I'll run for a while first and then take the bus."`},{zh:"他跑了很长时间，终于追上了那辆公共汽车。",py:"Tā pǎole hěn cháng shíjiān, zhōngyú zhuīshàngle nà liàng gōnggòng qìchē.",en:"He ran for a long time and finally caught up with the bus."},{zh:"他又问售票员：“这里到西湖多少钱？”",py:"Tā yòu wèn shòupiàoyuán: “Zhèlǐ dào Xīhú duōshao qián?”",en:'He asked the conductor again, "How much is it from here to West Lake?"'},{zh:"“五元。”",py:"“Wǔ yuán.”",en:'"Five yuan."'},{zh:"“天哪，方向错了！”",py:"“Tiān na, fāngxiàng cuò le!”",en:'"Oh no, I went the wrong way!"'}],vocab:[{w:"旅行",py:"lǚxíng",pos:"v.",en:"travel, go on a trip"},{w:"地方",py:"dìfang",pos:"n.",en:"place"},{w:"花",py:"huā",pos:"v.",en:"spend"},{w:"售票员",py:"shòupiàoyuán",pos:"n.",en:"ticket seller"},{w:"跑",py:"pǎo",pos:"v.",en:"run"},{w:"时间",py:"shíjiān",pos:"n.",en:"time"},{w:"天哪",py:"tiān na",pos:"interj.",en:"Dear me!"}],points:[{name:"终于",en:"finally, at last",eg:"他跑了很长时间，终于追上了那辆公共汽车。",egEn:"He ran for a long time and finally caught up with the bus.",zh:"“终于”，副词，表示经过很长时间或很多努力以后，最后出现了希望的结果。",enx:"“终于” is an adverb meaning “finally, at last”. It shows that a hoped-for result comes after a long time or a lot of effort.",egs:["（1）等了一个小时，公共汽车终于来了。","（2）我学了三年汉语，终于能看懂中文电影了。"]},{name:"追上",en:"catch up with",eg:"终于追上了那辆公共汽车。",egEn:"(He) finally caught up with that bus.",zh:"“追”是动词，意思是快走或快跑去赶前面的人或东西；“上”放在动词后面，表示达到了目的。“追上”就是追到了。",enx:"In “追上”, “追” is a verb meaning “to chase”, and “上” after it shows that the goal is reached. So “追上” means “to catch up with”.",egs:["（1）他跑得太快了，我追不上他。","（2）快跑，你还能追上他！"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"售票员骗（cheat）了王明明。",a:!1},{q:"王明明跑错方向了。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"王明明想（ ）去西湖。",options:["跑步","走路","坐公共汽车"],answer:2},{q:"王明明先跑一会儿，然后再坐公共汽车，是因为（ ）。",options:["西湖很近","他的钱不够了","车票太贵了"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"上有天堂，下有苏杭",titleEn:"Heaven Above, Suzhou and Hangzhou Below",zh:"中国人常说“上有天堂，下有苏杭”，意思是天上有天堂，地上有苏州和杭州，这两个地方像天堂一样美。苏州在江苏省，有很多有名的园林；杭州在浙江省，最有名的是西湖。这两个城市每年都有很多人去旅游。本课的王明明就是去杭州旅行的。",en:"Chinese people often say “Heaven above, Suzhou and Hangzhou below”, meaning that just as there is paradise in the sky, there are Suzhou and Hangzhou on earth — both as beautiful as paradise. Suzhou, in Jiangsu Province, has many famous classical gardens; Hangzhou, in Zhejiang Province, is best known for West Lake. Both cities attract many tourists every year. Wang Mingming in this lesson went on a trip to Hangzhou."}},{n:10,title:"座位在哪里？",py:"Zuòwèi zài nǎli?",en:"Where Are the Seats?",chars:163,daodu:"班上有12位同学，大家都坐在哪里？看看下面的话，你能帮钱小雪找到每个人的座位吗？",daoduEn:"There are 12 students in the class. Where does everyone sit? Read the clues — can you help Qian Xiaoxue find everyone’s seat?",paras:[{zh:"钱小雪是南京大学的留学生。班上有12位同学，6位男生，6位女生。6位男生是石川一郎、黄家友、金时元、赵书真、大卫和马克，6位女生是陈心宜、苏珊、安娜、和子、安丽秀和小雪。",py:"Qián Xiǎoxuě shì Nánjīng Dàxué de liúxuéshēng. Bān shang yǒu 12 wèi tóngxué, 6 wèi nánshēng, 6 wèi nǚshēng. 6 wèi nánshēng shì Shíchuān Yīláng, Huáng Jiāyǒu, Jīn Shíyuán, Zhào Shūzhēn, Dàwèi hé Mǎkè, 6 wèi nǚshēng shì Chén Xīnyí, Sūshān, Ānnà, Hézǐ, Ān Lìxiù hé Xiǎoxuě.",en:"Qian Xiaoxue is an international student at Nanjing University. There are 12 students in her class: 6 boys and 6 girls. The 6 boys are Ishikawa Ichiro, Huang Jiayou, Kim Siwon, Zhao Shuzhen, David and Mark. The 6 girls are Chen Xinyi, Susan, Anna, Kazuko, An Lixiu and Xiaoxue."},{zh:"赵书真的左边是黄家友，后边是大卫；苏珊的后边是金时元；安丽秀的左边是陈心宜，右边是马克，和子的右边是钱小雪。请你把他们的名字写在表格中。",py:"Zhào Shūzhēn de zuǒbian shì Huáng Jiāyǒu, hòubian shì Dàwèi; Sūshān de hòubian shì Jīn Shíyuán; Ān Lìxiù de zuǒbian shì Chén Xīnyí, yòubian shì Mǎkè, Hézǐ de yòubian shì Qián Xiǎoxuě. Qǐng nǐ bǎ tāmen de míngzi xiě zài biǎogé zhōng.",en:"To Zhao Shuzhen's left is Huang Jiayou, and behind him is David. Behind Susan is Kim Siwon. To An Lixiu's left is Chen Xinyi, and to her right is Mark. To Kazuko's right is Qian Xiaoxue. Please write their names in the table."},{zh:"第1行：空位｜赵书真｜苏珊",py:"Dì 1 háng: kòngwèi | Zhào Shūzhēn | Sūshān",en:"Row 1: empty seat | Zhao Shuzhen | Susan",fmt:"table"},{zh:"第2行：石川一郎｜空位｜空位",py:"Dì 2 háng: Shíchuān Yīláng | kòngwèi | kòngwèi",en:"Row 2: Ishikawa Ichiro | empty seat | empty seat",fmt:"table"},{zh:"第3行：空位｜安丽秀｜空位",py:"Dì 3 háng: kòngwèi | Ān Lìxiù | kòngwèi",en:"Row 3: empty seat | An Lixiu | empty seat",fmt:"table"},{zh:"第4行：安娜｜和子｜钱小雪",py:"Dì 4 háng: Ānnà | Hézǐ | Qián Xiǎoxuě",en:"Row 4: Anna | Kazuko | Qian Xiaoxue",fmt:"table"}],vocab:[{w:"留学生",py:"liúxuéshēng",pos:"n.",en:"overseas student"},{w:"男生",py:"nánshēng",pos:"n.",en:"boy"},{w:"女生",py:"nǚshēng",pos:"n.",en:"girl"},{w:"左边",py:"zuǒbian",pos:"n.",en:"left"},{w:"后边",py:"hòubian",pos:"n.",en:"behind"},{w:"右边",py:"yòubian",pos:"n.",en:"right"},{w:"表格",py:"biǎogé",pos:"n.",en:"table, form"}],points:[{name:"有",en:"there be",eg:"班上有12位同学。",egEn:"There are 12 students in the class.",zh:"“有”，动词，可以表示存在，常用格式是“地方/时间+有+人/东西”，意思是在某个地方或时间有某人或某物。",enx:"The verb “有” can show existence. The pattern “place/time + 有 + people/things” means “there is/are … (somewhere / at some time)”.",egs:["（1）桌子上有一本书。","（2）我们学校有很多留学生。"]},{name:"请",en:"please, request",eg:"请你把他们的名字写在表格中。",egEn:"Please write their names in the table.",zh:"“请”，动词，用在句子开头，客气地让别人做某事，常说“请你……”。",enx:"The verb “请” is used at the beginning of a sentence to ask someone politely to do something, like “please”. It is often used as “请你……”.",egs:["（1）请你说慢一点儿。","（2）请大家把书打开。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"马克的座位在钱小雪前边。",a:!0},{q:"黄家友、赵书真和大卫都在第一排。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"钱小雪是（ ）的留学生。",options:["北京大学","南京大学","上海大学"],answer:1},{q:"（ ）都是男生。",options:["赵书真、大卫、和子","黄家友、大卫、马克","安娜、小雪、金时元"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"六朝古都——南京",titleEn:"The Capital of Six Dynasties in History—Nanjing",zh:"南京是江苏省的省会，在长江边上。历史上，先后有六个朝代在南京建都，所以人们叫它“六朝古都”。明朝刚开始的时候，首都也在南京。今天的南京是一个重要的经济、文化和教育中心，有很多大学，比如本课的南京大学。",en:"Nanjing, the capital of Jiangsu Province, lies on the Yangtze River. In history, six dynasties one after another made Nanjing their capital, so it is called “the ancient capital of six dynasties”. At the beginning of the Ming Dynasty, the capital was also in Nanjing. Today Nanjing is an important economic, cultural and educational centre with many universities, such as Nanjing University in this lesson."}},{n:11,title:"小声一点儿",py:"Xiǎoshēng yìdiǎnr",en:"Keep Your Voice Down",chars:118,daodu:"已经晚上十点了，乐乐还不想睡觉。爸爸想了一个办法：给他讲故事。最后，谁先睡着了呢？",daoduEn:"It’s already ten o’clock at night, and Lele still doesn’t want to go to bed. Dad has an idea: tell him a story. In the end, who will fall asleep first?",paras:[{zh:"乐乐是个爱玩儿的孩子。一天，已经晚上十点了，他还不想睡觉。",py:"Lèle shì gè ài wánr de háizi. Yì tiān, yǐjīng wǎnshang shí diǎn le, tā hái bù xiǎng shuìjiào.",en:"Lele is a kid who loves to play. One day it was already ten o'clock at night, and he still didn't want to go to bed."},{zh:"爸爸想让他早点儿休息，就说：“爸爸给你讲《西游记》的故事，好不好？”乐乐最喜欢听《西游记》了，他非常高兴。",py:"Bàba xiǎng ràng tā zǎo diǎnr xiūxi, jiù shuō: “Bàba gěi nǐ jiǎng “Xīyóu Jì” de gùshi, hǎo bu hǎo?” Lèle zuì xǐhuan tīng “Xīyóu Jì” le, tā fēicháng gāoxìng.",en:`Dad wanted him to go to sleep a bit earlier, so he said, "I'll tell you a story from Journey to the West, OK?" Journey to the West was Lele's favorite, so he was very happy.`},{zh:"一个小时以后，房间里非常安静，没有人说话了。",py:"Yí gè xiǎoshí yǐhòu, fángjiān li fēicháng ānjìng, méiyǒu rén shuōhuà le.",en:"An hour later the room was very quiet. Nobody was talking anymore."},{zh:"妈妈想，乐乐肯定睡着了。",py:"Māma xiǎng, Lèle kěndìng shuìzháo le.",en:"Mom thought Lele must be asleep."},{zh:"她打开乐乐的房门，问：“睡着了吗？”",py:"Tā dǎkāi Lèle de fángmén, wèn: “Shuìzháo le ma?”",en:`She opened Lele's door and asked, "Asleep?"`},{zh:"“爸爸睡着了，小声一点儿。”",py:"“Bàba shuìzháo le, xiǎoshēng yìdiǎnr.”",en:`"Dad's asleep. Keep your voice down."`}],vocab:[{w:"玩",py:"wán",pos:"v.",en:"play"},{w:"睡觉",py:"shuìjiào",pos:"v.",en:"sleep"},{w:"休息",py:"xiūxi",pos:"v.",en:"rest"},{w:"讲",py:"jiǎng",pos:"v.",en:"tell"},{w:"故事",py:"gùshi",pos:"n.",en:"story"},{w:"安静",py:"ānjìng",pos:"adj.",en:"quiet"},{w:"肯定",py:"kěndìng",pos:"adv.",en:"surely"},{w:"睡着",py:"shuìzháo",pos:"v.",en:"fall asleep"},{w:"打开",py:"dǎkāi",pos:"v.",en:"open"}],points:[{name:"爱",en:"love, be fond of",eg:"乐乐是个爱玩儿的孩子。",egEn:"Lele is a child who loves to play.",zh:"“爱”，动词，除了表示爱一个人以外，还可以表示很喜欢做某事，后面常跟动词，比如“爱玩儿”“爱看书”。",enx:"Besides “to love (someone)”, the verb “爱” can mean “to be fond of doing something”. It is often followed by a verb, e.g. “爱玩儿” (love playing), “爱看书” (love reading).",egs:["（1）我妹妹很爱唱歌。","（2）他不爱吃水果，只爱吃肉。"]},{name:"一点儿",en:"a little bit",eg:"爸爸睡着了，小声一点儿。",egEn:"Dad’s asleep — keep your voice down a little.",zh:"“一点儿”，数量词，表示数量少或程度低。放在形容词后面，常用来比较或者客气地提出要求，比如“小声一点儿”“快一点儿”。",enx:"“一点儿” is a quantifier meaning “a little”. Placed after an adjective, it makes a comparison or a polite request, e.g. “小声一点儿” (a little quieter), “快一点儿” (a bit faster).",egs:["（1）这件衣服太大了，有小一点儿的吗？","（2）时间不早了，我们快一点儿走吧。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"乐乐喜欢听《西游记》的故事。",a:!0},{q:"爸爸给乐乐讲故事的时候，乐乐睡着了。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"爸爸为什么给乐乐讲故事？",options:["爸爸喜欢讲故事","想让乐乐早点儿睡","妈妈没时间给乐乐讲故事"],answer:1},{q:"妈妈开门的时候，（ ）睡着了。",options:["没有人","乐乐","爸爸"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"《西游记》",titleEn:"Journey to the West",zh:"《西游记》是中国古代的“四大名著”之一，一般认为作者是明代的吴承恩。书里讲的是孙悟空、猪八戒和沙和尚保护唐僧去西天取经的故事，他们一路上经历了九九八十一难。孙悟空会七十二变，非常受孩子们喜欢。很多中国孩子都是听着《西游记》的故事长大的。",en:"Journey to the West is one of the “Four Great Classical Novels” of China. It is generally believed to have been written by Wu Cheng’en of the Ming Dynasty. It tells how Sun Wukong (the Monkey King), Zhu Bajie (Pigsy) and Sha Heshang (Sandy) protect the monk Tang Seng on his journey to the West to fetch Buddhist scriptures, going through eighty-one hardships on the way. Sun Wukong can change into seventy-two different forms and is much loved by children. Many Chinese children grow up listening to stories from Journey to the West."}},{n:12,title:"走错了",py:"Zǒucuò le",en:"Wrong Door",chars:102,daodu:"马东音家的水龙头坏了，修理工一直没来。今天终于有人敲门了，是修理工吗？",daoduEn:"The tap in Ma Dongyin’s home was broken, but the repairman never came. Today someone finally knocked on the door. Was it the repairman?",paras:[{zh:"马东音是我的好朋友。最近他们家的一个水龙头坏了，可是修理工一直没来。",py:"Mǎ Dōngyīn shì wǒ de hǎo péngyou. Zuìjìn tāmen jiā de yí gè shuǐlóngtóu huài le, kěshì xiūlǐgōng yìzhí méi lái.",en:"Ma Dongyin is my good friend. Recently a tap at his home broke, but the repairman still hadn't come."},{zh:"昨天上午9点，有人敲门。马东音的妈妈打开门，是一位修理工！她高兴地说：“太好了，您终于来了。我们已经等您三天了！”",py:"Zuótiān shàngwǔ 9 diǎn, yǒu rén qiāo mén. Mǎ Dōngyīn de māma dǎkāi mén, shì yí wèi xiūlǐgōng! Tā gāoxìng de shuō: “Tài hǎo le, nín zhōngyú lái le. Wǒmen yǐjīng děng nín sān tiān le!”",en:`Yesterday at 9 a.m., someone knocked at the door. Ma Dongyin's mother opened it — it was a repairman! She said happily, "Great, you're finally here. We've been waiting for you for three days!"`},{zh:"“对不起，我走错了。有一家已经等我一个月了，现在我得去那家！”",py:"“Duìbuqǐ, wǒ zǒucuò le. Yǒu yì jiā yǐjīng děng wǒ yí gè yuè le, xiànzài wǒ děi qù nà jiā!”",en:`"Sorry, I've come to the wrong place. There's a family that has been waiting for me for a month. I have to go there now!"`}],vocab:[{w:"水龙头",py:"shuǐlóngtóu",pos:"n.",en:"water tap"},{w:"坏",py:"huài",pos:"v.",en:"break down"},{w:"修理工",py:"xiūlǐgōng",pos:"n.",en:"repairman"},{w:"一直",py:"yìzhí",pos:"adv.",en:"all along"},{w:"敲门",py:"qiāomén",pos:"v.",en:"knock on the door"},{w:"对不起",py:"duìbuqǐ",pos:"expr.",en:"sorry"},{w:"得",py:"děi",pos:"v.",en:"have to"}],points:[{name:"最近",en:"recently",eg:"最近他们家的一个水龙头坏了。",egEn:"Recently a tap in their home broke.",zh:"“最近”，名词，指说话以前（或以后）不久的一段时间，常放在句子开头或主语后面。",enx:"“最近” is a noun meaning “recently, lately”, referring to a period shortly before (or after) the time of speaking. It usually comes at the beginning of a sentence or after the subject.",egs:["（1）你最近忙不忙？","（2）最近天气很冷，多穿点儿衣服。"]},{name:"打开",en:"open, turn on",eg:"马东音的妈妈打开门，是一位修理工！",egEn:"Ma Dongyin’s mother opened the door — it was a repairman!",zh:"“打开”，动词，意思是把关着的东西开开，比如“打开门”“打开书”；也可以表示让电视、电脑等开始工作。",enx:"“打开” is a verb meaning “to open” something that is closed, e.g. “打开门” (open the door), “打开书” (open the book). It can also mean “to turn on” a TV, a computer, etc.",egs:["（1）房间里很热，请打开窗户。","（2）他一回家就打开了电视。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"马东音和妈妈等了修理工一个月。",a:!1},{q:"修理工要先给别人修，然后才给马东音家修。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"修理工（ ）以后才来马东音家。",options:["一个月","三天","昨天"],answer:1},{q:"哪一个和“现在我得去那家”中的“得”一样（same）？",options:["我考试得了100分","他汉字写得很好","很晚了，我得回家了"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"钟点工",titleEn:"Hourly Workers",zh:"钟点工就是按小时拿工资的人。在中国的城市里，很多家庭工作很忙，就请钟点工来帮忙打扫房间、做饭、洗衣服，有的还帮忙照顾孩子和老人。钟点工一般不住在主人家里，做完工作就走，有的钟点工一天要去好几家工作。",en:"Hourly workers (钟点工) are people who are paid by the hour. In Chinese cities, many busy families hire hourly workers to help clean the house, cook and do the laundry; some also help look after children or elderly people. Hourly workers usually don’t live in their employers’ homes and leave once the work is done; some work for several families in one day."}},{n:13,title:"手机丢了",py:"Shǒujī diū le",en:"Lost Phones",chars:129,daodu:"丢了手机，真着急！这两个人都写了寻物启事（xúnwù qǐshì: lost-and-found notice）。他们的手机是什么样的？为什么对他们非常重要？",daoduEn:"Losing your phone is so stressful! These two people each wrote a lost-and-found notice. What do their phones look like? Why are the phones so important to them?",paras:[{zh:"一",py:"Yī",en:"1",fmt:"h"},{zh:"寻诺基亚5230黑色手机，这是女朋友送我的生日礼物，对我来说，非常重要。请尽快跟我联系，电话：1283692378，非常感谢！",py:"Xún Nuòjīyà 5230 hēisè shǒujī, zhè shì nǚpéngyou sòng wǒ de shēngrì lǐwù, duì wǒ lái shuō, fēicháng zhòngyào. Qǐng jǐnkuài gēn wǒ liánxì, diànhuà: 1283692378, fēicháng gǎnxiè!",en:"Looking for a black Nokia 5230 phone. It was a birthday present from my girlfriend, and it's very important to me. Please contact me as soon as possible. Phone: 1283692378. Thank you very much!"},{zh:"张果果",py:"Zhāng Guǒguǒ",en:"Zhang Guoguo",fmt:"sign"},{zh:"2010年6月27日",py:"2010 nián 6 yuè 27 rì",en:"June 27, 2010",fmt:"sign"},{zh:"二",py:"Èr",en:"2",fmt:"h"},{zh:"6月26号下午我在学校打篮球时，手机（夏新A310）放在地上，走的时候忘了。因为上面有很多重要的电话，所以希望捡到手机的好心人，能还给我。我会请客哦（有美女和帅哥同学一起哦），联系电话：88811209。",py:"6 yuè 26 hào xiàwǔ wǒ zài xuéxiào dǎ lánqiú shí, shǒujī (Xiàxīn A310) fàng zài dì shang, zǒu de shíhou wàng le. Yīnwèi shàngmian yǒu hěn duō zhòngyào de diànhuà, suǒyǐ xīwàng jiǎndào shǒujī de hǎoxīnrén, néng huán gěi wǒ. Wǒ huì qǐngkè o (yǒu měinǚ hé shuàigē tóngxué yìqǐ o), liánxì diànhuà: 88811209.",en:"On the afternoon of June 26, while I was playing basketball at school, I put my phone (an Amoi A310) on the ground and forgot it when I left. It has lots of important phone numbers in it, so I hope whoever kindly finds it will give it back to me. I'll treat you to a meal (and some good-looking classmates will come too!). Contact number: 88811209."},{zh:"李书晴",py:"Lǐ Shūqíng",en:"Li Shuqing",fmt:"sign"},{zh:"2010年6月27日",py:"2010 nián 6 yuè 27 rì",en:"June 27, 2010",fmt:"sign"}],vocab:[{w:"丢",py:"diū",pos:"v.",en:"lose"},{w:"寻",py:"xún",pos:"v.",en:"look for"},{w:"黑色",py:"hēisè",pos:"n.",en:"black"},{w:"礼物",py:"lǐwù",pos:"n.",en:"gift"},{w:"重要",py:"zhòngyào",pos:"adj.",en:"important"},{w:"篮球",py:"lánqiú",pos:"n.",en:"basketball"},{w:"捡",py:"jiǎn",pos:"v.",en:"pick up, find"},{w:"还",py:"huán",pos:"v.",en:"return"},{w:"请客",py:"qǐngkè",pos:"v.",en:"invite somebody to dinner"},{w:"帅哥",py:"shuàigē",pos:"n.",en:"handsome boy"},{w:"因为……所以",py:"yīnwèi…suǒyǐ",pos:"conj.",en:"because…therefore"}],points:[{name:"尽快",en:"as soon as possible",eg:"请尽快跟我联系。",egEn:"Please contact me as soon as possible.",zh:"“尽快”，副词，意思是尽量快一点儿、越快越好，常用在请别人做事的时候。",enx:"“尽快” is an adverb meaning “as soon as possible”. It is often used when asking someone to do something.",egs:["（1）你病了，要尽快去看医生。","（2）这件事很重要，请尽快告诉他。"]},{name:"联系",en:"contact, get/be in touch",eg:"请尽快跟我联系。",egEn:"Please get in touch with me as soon as possible.",zh:"“联系”，动词，意思是通过打电话、发短信、写信等和别人交流，常说“跟/和……联系”。",enx:"“联系” is a verb meaning “to contact, to get in touch with” someone by phone, text message, letter, etc. It is often used as “跟/和……联系”.",egs:["（1）我们很久没有联系了。","（2）有问题可以跟王老师联系。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"张果果的手机是红色的。",a:!1},{q:"李书晴的手机是打篮球时丢的。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"张果果的手机是（ ）送的。",options:["父母","朋友","女朋友"],answer:2},{q:"李书晴的手机很重要，因为手机（ ）。",options:["是他女朋友送的","是他的生日礼物","上面有很多重要的电话"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"手机在中国",titleEn:"Mobile Phones in China",zh:"1987年，中国有了第一个移动电话网。那时候手机又大又贵，人们叫它“大哥大”，有手机的人很少。后来，手机越来越便宜，用的人也越来越多。到2010年，中国的手机用户已经超过了7亿。今天，人们不但用手机打电话、发短信，还用它买东西、付钱。",en:"In 1987, China got its first mobile phone network. Back then mobile phones were big and expensive — people called them “大哥大” (big brother) — and very few people had one. Later, phones became cheaper and cheaper, and more and more people used them. By 2010, China had over 700 million mobile phone users. Today, people use their phones not only to make calls and send text messages, but also to shop and pay."}},{n:14,title:"古老的城市——西安",py:"Gǔlǎo de chéngshì — Xī'ān",en:"An Ancient City — Xi'an",chars:146,daodu:"西安是一个古老的城市。在西安，有什么好看的？有什么好吃的？跟“我”一起去看看吧！",daoduEn:"Xi’an is an ancient city. What is there to see in Xi’an? What is there to eat? Come and have a look with the writer!",paras:[{zh:"昨天晚上九点十分，我和韩国朋友赵京美一起，从北京坐火车去西安旅游。今天早上七点，我们到了西安。",py:"Zuótiān wǎnshang jiǔ diǎn shí fēn, wǒ hé Hánguó péngyou Zhào Jīngměi yìqǐ, cóng Běijīng zuò huǒchē qù Xī'ān lǚyóu. Jīntiān zǎoshang qī diǎn, wǒmen dàole Xī'ān.",en:"At ten past nine last night, my Korean friend Zhao Jingmei and I took the train from Beijing to Xi'an for a trip. We arrived in Xi'an at seven this morning."},{zh:"西安是一个古老的城市，非常漂亮。西安最有名的是兵马俑，他们已经在地下2000多年了。",py:"Xī'ān shì yí gè gǔlǎo de chéngshì, fēicháng piàoliang. Xī'ān zuì yǒumíng de shì bīngmǎyǒng, tāmen yǐjīng zài dìxià 2000 duō nián le.",en:"Xi'an is an ancient city, and it's very beautiful. The most famous thing in Xi'an is the Terracotta Army. The figures have been underground for more than 2,000 years."},{zh:"兵马俑非常多，我拍了很多照片，有车、有马，还有士兵。",py:"Bīngmǎyǒng fēicháng duō, wǒ pāile hěn duō zhàopiàn, yǒu chē, yǒu mǎ, hái yǒu shìbīng.",en:"There are lots and lots of terracotta figures. I took many photos — of chariots, horses and soldiers."},{zh:"西安的小吃也很有名。在小吃街，我们吃了面条和羊肉泡馍。赵京美是个美食家，她一直说：“好吃！真好吃！”",py:"Xī'ān de xiǎochī yě hěn yǒumíng. Zài xiǎochījiē, wǒmen chīle miàntiáo hé yángròu pàomó. Zhào Jīngměi shì gè měishíjiā, tā yìzhí shuō: “Hǎochī! Zhēn hǎochī!”",en:`Xi'an's snacks are famous too. On the snack street we ate noodles and yangrou paomo (bread soaked in mutton soup). Zhao Jingmei is a real foodie. She kept saying, "Delicious! So delicious!"`},{zh:"我们都很喜欢西安。",py:"Wǒmen dōu hěn xǐhuan Xī'ān.",en:"We both love Xi'an."}],vocab:[{w:"兵马俑",py:"bīngmǎyǒng",pos:"n.",en:"Terracotta Warriors and Horses"},{w:"地下",py:"dìxià",pos:"n.",en:"underground"},{w:"拍",py:"pāi",pos:"v.",en:"take a picture"},{w:"照片",py:"zhàopiàn",pos:"n.",en:"photo, picture"},{w:"士兵",py:"shìbīng",pos:"n.",en:"soldier, warrior"},{w:"小吃",py:"xiǎochī",pos:"n.",en:"snack"},{w:"面条",py:"miàntiáo",pos:"n.",en:"noodle"},{w:"羊肉泡馍",py:"yángròu pàomó",pos:"n.",en:"pita bread soaked in lamb soup"},{w:"美食家",py:"měishíjiā",pos:"n.",en:"gourmet"}],points:[{name:"和……一起",en:"together with",eg:"我和韩国朋友赵京美一起，从北京坐火车去西安旅游。",egEn:"My Korean friend Zhao Jingmei and I took the train together from Beijing to Xi’an.",zh:"“和……一起”表示几个人一块儿做某事，常用格式是“A和B一起+动词”。",enx:"“和……一起” means “together with”. It shows that people do something together. The usual pattern is “A和B一起 + verb”.",egs:["（1）周末我和朋友一起去看电影。","（2）你想和我们一起吃饭吗？"]},{name:"最",en:"most",eg:"西安最有名的是兵马俑。",egEn:"The most famous thing in Xi’an is the Terracotta Army.",zh:"“最”，副词，表示在一个范围里比较，超过所有别的人或东西，常放在形容词或“喜欢”等动词前面。",enx:"“最” is an adverb that forms the superlative: compared within a group, someone or something goes beyond all the others. It usually goes before an adjective or a verb like “喜欢”.",egs:["（1）他是我们班最高的学生。","（2）我最喜欢吃妈妈做的饭。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"我和赵京美坐飞机去西安旅行。",a:!1},{q:"兵马俑已经在地下很长时间了。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"西安最有名的是（ ）。",options:["兵马俑","羊肉泡馍","面条"],answer:0},{q:"“美食家”的意思是（ ）。",options:["吃得很多的人","喜欢小吃的人","很会品尝（taste）美食的人"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"兵马俑",titleEn:"The Terracotta Warriors and Horses",zh:"兵马俑在西安附近的秦始皇陵旁边。1974年，当地几个农民打井的时候，发现了它们。兵马俑和真人、真马差不多一样大，每个士兵的样子都不一样。到现在，它们已经在地下两千多年了。很多人叫它“世界第八大奇迹”，每年都有很多人来西安参观。",en:"The Terracotta Warriors and Horses stand beside the Mausoleum of Qin Shi Huang near Xi’an. In 1974, some local farmers discovered them while digging a well. The figures are about the size of real people and real horses, and every soldier looks different. They have been underground for more than two thousand years. Many people call them “the Eighth Wonder of the World”, and every year many visitors come to Xi’an to see them."}},{n:15,title:"漂亮的一个“点”",py:"Piàoliang de yí gè “diǎn”",en:'A Beautiful "Dot"',chars:146,daodu:"王献之七岁开始学书法，很多人都说他的字不错。可是，他的爸爸妈妈是怎么看的呢？",daoduEn:"Wang Xianzhi began learning calligraphy at the age of seven, and many people said his handwriting was good. But what did his father and mother think?",paras:[{zh:"王羲之是古代著名的书法家。",py:"Wáng Xīzhī shì gǔdài zhùmíng de shūfǎjiā.",en:"Wang Xizhi was a famous calligrapher of ancient times."},{zh:"他的儿子王献之七岁的时候开始学书法。几年以后，很多人说他的字不错。",py:"Tā de érzi Wáng Xiànzhī qī suì de shíhou kāishǐ xué shūfǎ. Jǐ nián yǐhòu, hěn duō rén shuō tā de zì búcuò.",en:"His son Wang Xianzhi began learning calligraphy at the age of seven. A few years later, many people said his writing was quite good."},{zh:"一天，献之把很多写好的字给爸爸看。爸爸一边看，一边摇头。",py:"Yì tiān, Xiànzhī bǎ hěn duō xiěhǎo de zì gěi bàba kàn. Bàba yìbiān kàn, yìbiān yáotóu.",en:"One day, Xianzhi showed his father a lot of characters he had written. As his father looked at them, he kept shaking his head."},{zh:"看到一个“大”字的时候，非常满意，就在“大”字下面加了一个点。",py:"Kàndào yí gè “dà” zì de shíhou, fēicháng mǎnyì, jiù zài “dà” zì xiàmian jiāle yí gè diǎn.",en:'When he came to the character 大 ("big"), he was very pleased, so he added a dot under it.'},{zh:"献之又拿给妈妈看。妈妈一边看，一边说：“这个‘太’，写得最好。”",py:"Xiànzhī yòu ná gěi māma kàn. Māma yìbiān kàn, yìbiān shuō: “Zhège ‘tài’, xiě de zuì hǎo.”",en:`Xianzhi then took them to show his mother. As she looked, she said, "This 太 is the best one." (The dot his father added turned 大 into 太 — so the best part was the father's dot.)`},{zh:"献之听了妈妈的话，很不好意思。他不再骄傲，努力练习，后来也成了著名的书法家。",py:"Xiànzhī tīngle māma de huà, hěn bù hǎoyìsi. Tā bú zài jiāo'ào, nǔlì liànxí, hòulái yě chéngle zhùmíng de shūfǎjiā.",en:"Hearing what his mother said, Xianzhi felt very embarrassed. He stopped being proud and practiced hard, and later he became a famous calligrapher too."}],vocab:[{w:"著名",py:"zhùmíng",pos:"adj.",en:"famous, well-known"},{w:"书法家",py:"shūfǎjiā",pos:"n.",en:"calligrapher"},{w:"给……看",py:"gěi…kàn",pos:"expr.",en:"show something to somebody"},{w:"一边……一边",py:"yìbiān…yìbiān",pos:"expr.",en:"while…while…"},{w:"摇头",py:"yáotóu",pos:"v.",en:"shake head"},{w:"加",py:"jiā",pos:"v.",en:"add"},{w:"不好意思",py:"bù hǎoyìsi",pos:"adj.",en:"embarrassed, ashamed"},{w:"骄傲",py:"jiāo'ào",pos:"adj.",en:"proud, conceited"}],points:[{name:"成",en:"become, turn into",eg:"他不再骄傲，努力练习，后来也成了著名的书法家。",egEn:"He was no longer conceited, practiced hard, and later also became a famous calligrapher.",zh:"“成”，动词，表示变为、成为，后面常跟名词，比如“成了书法家”“成了好朋友”。",enx:"“成” is a verb meaning “to become, to turn into”. It is usually followed by a noun, e.g. “成了书法家” (became a calligrapher), “成了好朋友” (became good friends).",egs:["（1）我们在中国认识，后来成了好朋友。","（2）天太冷了，水都成了冰。"]},{name:"满意",en:"satisfied",eg:"看到一个“大”字的时候，非常满意。",egEn:"When he saw one character “大”, he was very pleased.",zh:"“满意”，形容词，表示觉得很好，和自己想的一样，常说“对……很满意”。",enx:"“满意” is an adjective meaning “satisfied, pleased”. It is often used as “对……很满意” (be satisfied with …).",egs:["（1）老师对我的作业很满意。","（2）这个房间又大又便宜，我很满意。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"王献之的爸爸是一位著名的书法家。",a:!0},{q:"爸爸对儿子的字都很满意。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"“大”字下面加上一点是（ ）。",options:["犬","太","不"],answer:1},{q:"妈妈认为献之的（ ）写得最好。",options:["大","太","大字下面的“、”"],answer:2}],tip:{title:"中国书法",titleEn:"Chinese Calligraphy",zh:"书法是中国特有的一种传统艺术，就是用毛笔写汉字的艺术。中国人用毛笔写字已经有很长的历史了。书法有好几种字体，比如楷书、行书、草书等。本课的王羲之是东晋时候的书法家，人们叫他“书圣”；他的儿子王献之也是著名的书法家。",en:"Calligraphy is a traditional art unique to China — the art of writing Chinese characters with a brush. The Chinese have written with brushes for a very long time. Calligraphy has several styles of script, such as regular script, running script and cursive script. Wang Xizhi in this lesson was a calligrapher of the Eastern Jin Dynasty, known as “the Sage of Calligraphy”; his son Wang Xianzhi was also a famous calligrapher."}},{n:16,title:"通知",py:"Tōngzhī",en:"Notice",chars:99,daodu:"你喜欢打羽毛球吗？中文系有羽毛球活动。活动在什么时候？要交多少钱？看看这个通知吧。",daoduEn:"Do you like playing badminton? The Chinese Department has badminton sessions. When are they? How much does it cost? Read this notice.",paras:[{zh:"大家好！",py:"Dàjiā hǎo!",en:"Hello, everyone!"},{zh:"羽毛球活动时间为每个星期二、四下午4:00—6:00，每个星期三中午12:30—13:30。",py:"Yǔmáoqiú huódòng shíjiān wéi měi gè xīngqī'èr, sì xiàwǔ 4:00-6:00, měi gè xīngqīsān zhōngwǔ 12:30-13:30.",en:"Badminton sessions are every Tuesday and Thursday, 4:00-6:00 p.m., and every Wednesday at noon, 12:30-13:30."},{zh:"会费每人每年30元，用来买羽毛球，请交给王兰兰老师。",py:"Huìfèi měi rén měi nián 30 yuán, yònglái mǎi yǔmáoqiú, qǐng jiāo gěi Wáng Lánlán lǎoshī.",en:"The membership fee is 30 yuan per person per year, used to buy shuttlecocks. Please pay it to Ms. Wang Lanlan."},{zh:"下个星期的活动时间：",py:"Xià gè xīngqī de huódòng shíjiān:",en:"Next week's sessions:"},{zh:"3月16日（星期二）下午4:00—6:00，两块场地。",py:"3 yuè 16 rì (xīngqī'èr) xiàwǔ 4:00-6:00, liǎng kuài chǎngdì.",en:"March 16 (Tuesday), 4:00-6:00 p.m., two courts.",fmt:"table"},{zh:"3月17日（星期三）中午12:30—13:30，一块场地。",py:"3 yuè 17 rì (xīngqīsān) zhōngwǔ 12:30-13:30, yí kuài chǎngdì.",en:"March 17 (Wednesday), noon, 12:30-13:30, one court.",fmt:"table"},{zh:"3月18日（星期四）下午4:00—6:00，两块场地。",py:"3 yuè 18 rì (xīngqīsì) xiàwǔ 4:00-6:00, liǎng kuài chǎngdì.",en:"March 18 (Thursday), 4:00-6:00 p.m., two courts.",fmt:"table"},{zh:"欢迎参加！",py:"Huānyíng cānjiā!",en:"Everyone is welcome!"},{zh:"中文系",py:"Zhōngwénxì",en:"Chinese Department",fmt:"sign"},{zh:"2010年3月14日",py:"2010 nián 3 yuè 14 rì",en:"March 14, 2010",fmt:"sign"}],vocab:[{w:"星期",py:"xīngqī",pos:"n.",en:"week"},{w:"会费",py:"huìfèi",pos:"n.",en:"membership fee"},{w:"用来",py:"yònglái",pos:"v.",en:"be used for"},{w:"交",py:"jiāo",pos:"v.",en:"give, hand over"},{w:"场地",py:"chǎngdì",pos:"n.",en:"court, site"},{w:"系",py:"xì",pos:"n.",en:"department"}],points:[{name:"每",en:"every, each",eg:"会费每人每年30元。",egEn:"The membership fee is 30 yuan per person per year.",zh:"“每”，代词，指全部中的任何一个，常说“每+量词+名词”，比如“每个人”“每年”，后面常有“都”。",enx:"“每” is a pronoun meaning “every, each”, referring to any one of a whole group. It is usually used as “每 + measure word + noun”, e.g. “每个人” (everyone), “每年” (every year), and is often followed by “都”.",egs:["（1）我每天早上七点起床。","（2）每个学生都有一本汉语书。"]},{name:"欢迎",en:"welcome",eg:"欢迎参加！",egEn:"Everyone is welcome to join!",zh:"“欢迎”，动词，表示很高兴地迎接别人，或者很高兴别人来参加、来做客，常说“欢迎你”“欢迎参加”。",enx:"“欢迎” is a verb meaning “to welcome”. It expresses gladness at receiving someone or at someone coming to join in, e.g. “欢迎你” (welcome), “欢迎参加” (you’re welcome to join).",egs:["（1）欢迎你来我家玩儿！","（2）欢迎大家来中国旅行。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"每个人星期二、三、四都有羽毛球活动。",a:!0},{q:"下个星期二的羽毛球活动有两块场地。",a:!0}],mc:[],tip:{title:"大学生社团",titleEn:"College Student Communities",zh:"中国的大学里有很多学生社团。喜欢唱歌的同学可以参加合唱团，喜欢跳舞的可以参加舞蹈团，喜欢运动的可以参加乒乓球俱乐部、羽毛球协会、登山协会等，还有爱心社、天文社等。参加社团能认识很多新朋友，也能让大学生活更有意思。",en:"Chinese universities have many student clubs. Students who like singing can join a choir, those who like dancing can join a dance troupe, and those who like sports can join a table tennis club, a badminton association, a mountaineering association and so on. There are also volunteer clubs, astronomy clubs and more. Joining a club is a good way to make new friends and makes university life more interesting."}},{n:17,title:"冰糖葫芦",py:"Bīngtáng húlu",en:"Candied Haws on a Stick",chars:132,daodu:"“我”小时候就喜欢吃冰糖葫芦。有一天，明明拿着一串冰糖葫芦来了，“我”想出了一个好主意……",daoduEn:"As a child, the writer loved sugar-coated haws. One day, Mingming came over holding a stick of them, and the writer came up with a clever idea…",paras:[{zh:"我小时候就喜欢吃冰糖葫芦。",py:"Wǒ xiǎo shíhou jiù xǐhuan chī bīngtáng húlu.",en:"Even as a child I loved eating candied haws on a stick."},{zh:"八岁那年，有一天，我正在家里做作业，明明拿着一串冰糖葫芦过来了。看着好吃的冰糖葫芦，我突然想出了一个主意。",py:"Bā suì nà nián, yǒu yì tiān, wǒ zhèngzài jiā li zuò zuòyè, Míngmíng názhe yí chuàn bīngtáng húlu guòlai le. Kànzhe hǎochī de bīngtáng húlu, wǒ tūrán xiǎngchūle yí gè zhǔyi.",en:"The year I was eight, one day I was doing my homework at home when Mingming came over holding a stick of candied haws. Looking at those tasty candied haws, I suddenly came up with an idea."},{zh:"我拿着冰糖葫芦，问他：“这上面有10个山楂，吃了1个还有几个？”我拿下一个山楂放到嘴里。",py:"Wǒ názhe bīngtáng húlu, wèn tā: “Zhè shàngmian yǒu 10 gè shānzhā, chīle 1 gè hái yǒu jǐ gè?” Wǒ ná xià yí gè shānzhā fàngdào zuǐ li.",en:'I took the candied haws and asked him, "There are 10 haws on here. If you eat 1, how many are left?" I pulled one haw off and put it in my mouth.'},{zh:"“9个！”“对，明明真聪明！”",py:"“9 gè!” “Duì, Míngmíng zhēn cōngming!”",en:`"Nine!" "Right! Mingming, you're so smart!"`},{zh:"再吃掉1个呢？“8个！”很快，山楂变成了5个。这时，明明看着冰糖葫芦，突然大声地哭起来……",py:"Zài chīdiào 1 gè ne? “8 gè!” Hěn kuài, shānzhā biànchéngle 5 gè. Zhè shí, Míngmíng kànzhe bīngtáng húlu, tūrán dàshēng de kū qǐlai...",en:'And if I eat 1 more? "Eight!" Soon there were only 5 haws left. Just then Mingming looked at the candied haws and suddenly burst out crying loudly...'}],vocab:[{w:"作业",py:"zuòyè",pos:"n.",en:"homework"},{w:"串",py:"chuàn",pos:"m.",en:"a stick of"},{w:"山楂",py:"shānzhā",pos:"n.",en:"haw"},{w:"拿",py:"ná",pos:"v.",en:"hold"},{w:"嘴",py:"zuǐ",pos:"n.",en:"mouth"},{w:"聪明",py:"cōngming",pos:"adj.",en:"clever, bright"},{w:"这时",py:"zhèshí",pos:"pron.",en:"at this time"},{w:"大声",py:"dàshēng",pos:"adv.",en:"loudly"},{w:"哭",py:"kū",pos:"v.",en:"cry"}],points:[{name:"主意",en:"idea",eg:"看着好吃的冰糖葫芦，我突然想出了一个主意。",egEn:"Looking at the tasty sugar-coated haws, I suddenly came up with an idea.",zh:"“主意”，名词，指办法、想法，常说“想出一个主意”“好主意”。",enx:"“主意” is a noun meaning “idea, plan”. Common expressions are “想出一个主意” (come up with an idea) and “好主意” (good idea).",egs:["（1）我们周末去爬山，怎么样？——好主意！","（2）我不知道买什么礼物，你帮我出个主意吧。"]},{name:"变成",en:"become, turn into",eg:"很快，山楂变成了5个。",egEn:"Very soon, the haws went down to five.",zh:"“变成”，动词，表示一种东西或情况经过变化，成了另一种东西或情况，后面常跟名词或数量词。",enx:"“变成” is a verb meaning “to become, to turn into”. It shows that something changes into something else, and is usually followed by a noun or a number phrase.",egs:["（1）秋天到了，树叶变成了黄色。","（2）十年过去了，那个小孩儿变成了大学生。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"我八岁的时候开始喜欢吃冰糖葫芦。",a:!1},{q:"我一共吃了6个山楂。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"看着好吃的糖葫芦，我想出了一个主意，可以（ ）。",options:["吃到明明的糖葫芦","帮助明明学习","让明明哭"],answer:0},{q:"明明看着糖葫芦，突然大声地哭起来，因为（ ）。",options:["他不会回答问题","糖葫芦只有5个了","糖葫芦不好吃"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"北方小吃——冰糖葫芦",titleEn:"Sugar-Coated Haws, a Snack in Northern China",zh:"冰糖葫芦是中国北方的传统小吃，在北京特别有名。做法是把山楂一个一个串在竹签上，再放进熬好的糖里，等糖变冷、变硬就可以吃了。冰糖葫芦吃起来又酸又甜。冬天的时候，街上常常能看到卖冰糖葫芦的人。现在除了山楂，也有用草莓等水果做的。",en:"Sugar-coated haws are a traditional snack of northern China, especially famous in Beijing. To make them, haws are put one by one on a bamboo stick and dipped in hot sugar syrup; once the sugar cools and hardens, they are ready to eat. They taste both sour and sweet. In winter you often see people selling them on the street. Nowadays, besides haws, they are also made with strawberries and other fruit."}},{n:18,title:"马大哈",py:"Mǎdàhā",en:"Absent-Minded",chars:127,daodu:"黄家友是一个聪明、认真的医生，可是在生活中，他有点儿马大哈。“马大哈”是什么样的人呢？",daoduEn:"Huang Jiayou is a clever and conscientious doctor, but in daily life he is a bit of a scatterbrain (马大哈). What kind of person is a 马大哈?",paras:[{zh:"黄家友是个非常聪明的医生，个子很高，长得很帅，工作非常认真。可他在生活中却有点儿马大哈，总是丢东西，特别是丢伞。",py:"Huáng Jiāyǒu shì gè fēicháng cōngming de yīshēng, gèzi hěn gāo, zhǎng de hěn shuài, gōngzuò fēicháng rènzhēn. Kě tā zài shēnghuó zhōng què yǒudiǎnr mǎdàhā, zǒngshì diū dōngxi, tèbié shì diū sǎn.",en:"Huang Jiayou is a very smart doctor. He's tall and handsome, and he works very conscientiously. But in everyday life he's a bit absent-minded. He's always losing things, especially umbrellas."},{zh:"他每次出门，只要带伞，回来的时候伞就没了。每次他丢了伞，妻子就会很不高兴。",py:"Tā měi cì chūmén, zhǐyào dài sǎn, huílai de shíhou sǎn jiù méi le. Měi cì tā diūle sǎn, qīzi jiù huì hěn bù gāoxìng.",en:"Every time he goes out with an umbrella, it's gone by the time he comes back. Every time he loses an umbrella, his wife gets very upset."},{zh:"有一天下班回家，黄家友拿着一把伞，高兴地对妻子说：“你看，伞在这儿呢。”",py:"Yǒu yì tiān xiàbān huíjiā, Huáng Jiāyǒu názhe yì bǎ sǎn, gāoxìng de duì qīzi shuō: “Nǐ kàn, sǎn zài zhèr ne.”",en:`One day he came home from work holding an umbrella and said happily to his wife, "Look, here's the umbrella."`},{zh:"妻子笑着说：“今天你出去的时候没有带伞！”",py:"Qīzi xiàozhe shuō: “Jīntiān nǐ chūqù de shíhou méiyǒu dài sǎn!”",en:`His wife laughed and said, "You didn't take an umbrella when you went out today!"`}],vocab:[{w:"个子",py:"gèzi",pos:"n.",en:"height"},{w:"认真",py:"rènzhēn",pos:"adj.",en:"conscientious, earnest"},{w:"总是",py:"zǒngshì",pos:"adv.",en:"always"},{w:"东西",py:"dōngxi",pos:"n.",en:"thing"},{w:"特别",py:"tèbié",pos:"adv.",en:"especially"},{w:"伞",py:"sǎn",pos:"n.",en:"umbrella"},{w:"每次",py:"měicì",pos:"adv.",en:"every time"},{w:"妻子",py:"qīzi",pos:"n.",en:"wife"}],points:[{name:"特别是",en:"especially, in particular",eg:"他总是丢东西，特别是丢伞。",egEn:"He is always losing things, especially umbrellas.",zh:"“特别是”用来在前面说的范围里，再特别提出一部分，表示这一部分更突出，常放在句子后一部分的开头。",enx:"“特别是” means “especially, in particular”. It singles out one part of what was mentioned before to emphasize it, usually at the beginning of the second part of a sentence.",egs:["（1）我喜欢运动，特别是游泳。","（2）北京的冬天很冷，特别是晚上。"]},{name:"只要……就",en:"as long as",eg:"他每次出门，只要带伞，回来的时候伞就没了。",egEn:"Every time he goes out, as long as he takes an umbrella, it’s gone by the time he comes back.",zh:"“只要……就……”，“只要”后面说一个条件，“就”后面说结果，表示有了这个条件，就一定会有这个结果。",enx:"“只要……就……” means “as long as … then …”. “只要” introduces a condition and “就” introduces the result, showing that once the condition is met, the result will follow.",egs:["（1）只要你努力，就能学好汉语。","（2）只要有时间，我就去打篮球。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"黄家友在工作中有点儿马大哈。",a:!1},{q:"黄家友把别人的伞拿回家了。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"他工作非常认真，（ ）。",options:["很少出错","总是忘记做一些重要的事情"],answer:0},{q:"他在生活中有点儿马大哈，（ ）。",options:["做事很粗心（careless）","很少丢东西"],answer:0}],tip:{title:"三字俗语",titleEn:"Three-Character Sayings",zh:"汉语里有很多三个字的俗语，它们的意思常常和字面意思不一样。比如“马大哈”，说的是做事很粗心的人，和马没有关系；“夜猫子”说的是晚上很晚还不睡觉的人；“铁公鸡”说的是一分钱也不愿意花的人；“二百五”是说人傻的话，不太礼貌，最好别用。",en:"Chinese has many three-character sayings whose meanings often differ from their literal meanings. For example, “马大哈” describes a careless person and has nothing to do with horses; “夜猫子” (night cat) is someone who stays up very late; “铁公鸡” (iron rooster) is someone who won’t spend a single cent; and “二百五” (two hundred and fifty) calls someone stupid — it is rude, so better not use it."}},{n:19,title:"小马过河",py:"Xiǎo mǎ guò hé",en:"The Little Horse Crosses the River",chars:139,daodu:"小马要过河，可是不知道河水深不深。牛爷爷说不深，小松鼠说很深。小马应该听谁的呢？",daoduEn:"The little horse wants to cross the river, but he doesn’t know how deep the water is. Grandpa Ox says it isn’t deep; the little squirrel says it’s very deep. Whom should the little horse listen to?",paras:[{zh:"一只小马要过河，可是不知道河水的深浅。他就问老牛：“牛爷爷，河水深吗？”老牛说：“不深，不深。”",py:"Yì zhī xiǎo mǎ yào guò hé, kěshì bù zhīdào hé shuǐ de shēnqiǎn. Tā jiù wèn lǎo niú: “Niú yéye, hé shuǐ shēn ma?” Lǎo niú shuō: “Bù shēn, bù shēn.”",en:`A little horse wanted to cross a river, but he didn't know how deep the water was. So he asked an old ox, "Grandpa Ox, is the river deep?" The old ox said, "Not deep, not deep."`},{zh:"小马来到河边，他刚要过河，小松鼠说：“小马，别下去，河水非常深！昨天我的一个朋友就掉进河里了。”",py:"Xiǎo mǎ láidào hébiān, tā gāng yào guò hé, xiǎo sōngshǔ shuō: “Xiǎo mǎ, bié xiàqu, hé shuǐ fēicháng shēn! Zuótiān wǒ de yí gè péngyou jiù diàojìn hé li le.”",en:`The little horse came to the riverbank. Just as he was about to cross, a little squirrel said, "Little horse, don't go in! The river is very deep! Yesterday one of my friends fell in."`},{zh:"老牛说河水浅，小松鼠说河水深，怎么办？小马只好回家问妈妈。妈妈和小马一起来到河边，她让小马自己试一试。",py:"Lǎo niú shuō hé shuǐ qiǎn, xiǎo sōngshǔ shuō hé shuǐ shēn, zěnme bàn? Xiǎo mǎ zhǐhǎo huíjiā wèn māma. Māma hé xiǎo mǎ yìqǐ láidào hébiān, tā ràng xiǎo mǎ zìjǐ shì yi shì.",en:"The old ox said the river was shallow, the little squirrel said it was deep — what should he do? The little horse had to go home and ask his mother. His mother came to the river with him and let him try it himself."},{zh:"小马试了试，河水不深也不浅，他高兴地过了河。",py:"Xiǎo mǎ shìle shì, hé shuǐ bù shēn yě bù qiǎn, tā gāoxìng de guòle hé.",en:"The little horse tried it. The river was neither deep nor shallow, and he happily crossed it."}],vocab:[{w:"深",py:"shēn",pos:"adj.",en:"deep"},{w:"浅",py:"qiǎn",pos:"adj.",en:"shallow"},{w:"松鼠",py:"sōngshǔ",pos:"n.",en:"squirrel"},{w:"别",py:"bié",pos:"adv.",en:"don't"},{w:"下去",py:"xiàqù",pos:"v.",en:"go down"},{w:"掉",py:"diào",pos:"v.",en:"fall"}],points:[{name:"怎么办",en:"how to deal with it",eg:"老牛说河水浅，小松鼠说河水深，怎么办？",egEn:"Grandpa Ox says the water is shallow and the little squirrel says it’s deep. What should he do?",zh:"“怎么办”，用来问遇到问题或困难的时候应该怎么做，可以单独用，也可以放在句子后面。",enx:"“怎么办” asks what one should do when facing a problem or difficulty (“What should I do?”). It can be used on its own or at the end of a sentence.",egs:["（1）我的钱包丢了，怎么办？","（2）明天下雨的话，我们怎么办？"]},{name:"试一试",en:"try",eg:"她让小马自己试一试。",egEn:"She let the little horse try it himself.",zh:"“试”是动词，意思是为了看看结果先做一做。单音节动词可以重叠成“V一V”，比如“试一试”“看一看”，表示动作时间短，或者轻松地试着做。",enx:"“试” is a verb meaning “to try”. One-syllable verbs can be repeated as “V一V”, e.g. “试一试”, “看一看”, meaning doing something briefly or trying it out.",egs:["（1）这件衣服很漂亮，你试一试吧。","（2）这个字怎么写？让我想一想。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"因为不知道河水深浅，所以小马不敢过河。",a:!0},{q:"牛爷爷说河水不深，他是在骗（cheat）小马。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"小马回家问妈妈河水深不深，妈妈让小马（ ）。",options:["自己试一试","问牛爷爷","问小松鼠"],answer:0},{q:"（ ）觉得河水很深，因为她的一个朋友昨天掉进河里了。",options:["牛爷爷","小松鼠","小马"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"《小马过河》",titleEn:"A Little Horse Crosses the River",zh:"《小马过河》是一个很有名的中国童话，写于20世纪50年代，很长时间都在中国小学的语文书里，很多中国人小时候都读过。它告诉我们：别人的话可以听，但是不能什么都听别人的，因为每个人的情况不一样。遇到问题，要自己想一想、试一试。",en:"A Little Horse Crosses the River is a well-known Chinese fable written in the 1950s. For a long time it was in Chinese primary school textbooks, and many Chinese people read it as children. It teaches us that we can listen to what others say, but we shouldn’t simply follow everyone’s advice, because each person’s situation is different. When we meet a problem, we should think it over and try it ourselves."}},{n:20,title:"一点儿",py:"Yìdiǎnr",en:"Just a Little",chars:146,daodu:"马克刚到中国，还不太会说汉语。他去理发，只跟理发师说了“一点儿”。理发师能明白他的意思吗？",daoduEn:"Mark has just arrived in China and can’t speak much Chinese yet. He goes for a haircut and only says “一点儿” (a little) to the barber. Will the barber understand what he means?",paras:[{zh:"有一个外国人，名字叫马克，他今年五十多岁了。因为刚到中国一个月，他还不太会说汉语。",py:"Yǒu yí gè wàiguórén, míngzi jiào Mǎkè, tā jīnnián wǔshí duō suì le. Yīnwèi gāng dào Zhōngguó yí gè yuè, tā hái bú tài huì shuō Hànyǔ.",en:"There was a foreigner named Mark, who was in his fifties. He had arrived in China only a month before, so he still couldn't speak much Chinese."},{zh:"一天他想理发，但是又不希望头发太短。到了理发店以后，他一边跟理发师说“一点儿”，一边做出理发的样子。理发师好像听懂了，一边说“OK”，一边开始理发。",py:"Yì tiān tā xiǎng lǐfà, dànshì yòu bù xīwàng tóufa tài duǎn. Dàole lǐfàdiàn yǐhòu, tā yìbiān gēn lǐfàshī shuō “yìdiǎnr”, yìbiān zuòchū lǐfà de yàngzi. Lǐfàshī hǎoxiàng tīngdǒng le, yìbiān shuō “OK”, yìbiān kāishǐ lǐfà.",en:`One day he wanted a haircut, but he didn't want his hair too short. At the barbershop he said "yìdiǎnr" ("a little") to the barber while miming a haircut. The barber seemed to understand. Saying "OK," he started cutting.`},{zh:"那天马克非常累，刚坐下就睡着了。二十分钟后理发师说“OK了”，马克看着镜子里的自己，哭笑不得。因为他的头发只有一点儿了！",py:"Nà tiān Mǎkè fēicháng lèi, gāng zuòxia jiù shuìzháo le. Èrshí fēnzhōng hòu lǐfàshī shuō “OK le”, Mǎkè kànzhe jìngzi li de zìjǐ, kūxiào bù dé. Yīnwèi tā de tóufa zhǐ yǒu yìdiǎnr le!",en:`Mark was very tired that day and fell asleep as soon as he sat down. Twenty minutes later the barber said, "OK, done." Looking at himself in the mirror, Mark didn't know whether to laugh or cry — because now he had only a little hair left!`}],vocab:[{w:"理发",py:"lǐfà",pos:"v.",en:"have one's hair cut"},{w:"头发",py:"tóufa",pos:"n.",en:"hair"},{w:"短",py:"duǎn",pos:"adj.",en:"short"},{w:"理发师",py:"lǐfàshī",pos:"n.",en:"hairdresser"},{w:"样子",py:"yàngzi",pos:"n.",en:"look, gesture"},{w:"懂",py:"dǒng",pos:"v.",en:"understand"},{w:"累",py:"lèi",pos:"adj.",en:"tired"},{w:"镜子",py:"jìngzi",pos:"n.",en:"mirror"}],points:[{name:"好像",en:"seem to, it seems that",eg:"理发师好像听懂了。",egEn:"The barber seemed to understand.",zh:"“好像”，副词，表示不太肯定，觉得可能是这样，意思和“似乎”“大概”差不多。",enx:"“好像” is an adverb meaning “seem, it seems that”. It shows the speaker is not quite sure, similar to “似乎” or “大概”.",egs:["（1）外面好像下雨了。","（2）我好像在哪儿见过他。"]},{name:"哭笑不得",en:"do not know whether to cry or laugh",eg:"马克看着镜子里的自己，哭笑不得。",egEn:"Looking at himself in the mirror, Mark didn’t know whether to laugh or cry.",zh:"“哭笑不得”，成语，意思是哭也不好，笑也不好，形容遇到了让人很尴尬、没有办法的事情。",enx:"“哭笑不得” is an idiom meaning “not knowing whether to laugh or cry”. It describes being in an awkward, helpless situation.",egs:["（1）他把盐当成糖放进了咖啡里，真让人哭笑不得。","（2）孩子的话让妈妈哭笑不得。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"马克刚到中国一个月，他只会说一点儿汉语。",a:!0},{q:"理发师明白了马克的意思。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"马克想理发，他（ ）。",options:["不想头发只有一点儿","希望头发很短"],answer:0},{q:"马克看着镜子里的自己，哭笑不得，因为（ ）。",options:["他很喜欢自己的新发型","他的头发只有一点儿了"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"二月二，龙抬头",titleEn:"The Dragon Raises Its Head (2nd Day of the 2nd Lunar Month)",zh:"农历二月初二叫“龙抬头”，是中国的一个传统节日。这时候天气变暖，春天来了。民间有一个习俗：正月里很多人不理发，到了二月二再去理发，叫“剃龙头”，人们觉得这一天理发能带来好运气。所以每年这一天，理发店里的人特别多。",en:"The second day of the second lunar month is called “the Dragon Raises Its Head”, a traditional Chinese festival. At this time the weather turns warm and spring arrives. There is a folk custom: many people don’t get a haircut during the first lunar month and wait until this day, which is called “shaving the dragon’s head”. People believe a haircut on this day brings good luck, so barbershops are especially busy every year on this day."}},{n:21,title:"前门儿≠前门儿",py:"Qiánménr ≠ qiánménr",en:"Qianmen(r) ≠ Front Gate",chars:108,daodu:"爱子很喜欢用儿化音。可是，“前门”后面加上一个“儿”，意思还一样吗？",daoduEn:"Aiko loves using the “-r” ending (儿化音). But if you add “儿” after “前门” (Qianmen), does it still mean the same thing?",paras:[{zh:"爱子是日本留学生，她汉语学得很好。她还很喜欢用儿化音，但是有一次闹了笑话。",py:"Àizǐ shì Rìběn liúxuéshēng, tā Hànyǔ xué de hěn hǎo. Tā hái hěn xǐhuan yòng érhuàyīn, dànshì yǒu yí cì nàole xiàohua.",en:'Aiko is an international student from Japan. Her Chinese is very good. She also loves using the "-r" sound (érhuà), but once it made her look silly.'},{zh:"那一天，爱子想去天安门附近的前门玩儿。她在宿舍门口跟出租车司机说：“我要去前门儿。”",py:"Nà yì tiān, Àizǐ xiǎng qù Tiān'ānmén fùjìn de Qiánmén wánr. Tā zài sùshè ménkǒu gēn chūzūchē sījī shuō: “Wǒ yào qù Qiánménr.”",en:`That day Aiko wanted to go to Qianmen, near Tian'anmen Square, for some fun. At the door of her dorm she told a taxi driver, "I want to go to Qianmenr."`},{zh:"很快，司机告诉她：“前门儿到了。”爱子很奇怪，为什么这么快呢？原来，司机把她送到了大学的前门儿。",py:"Hěn kuài, sījī gàosu tā: “Qiánménr dào le.” Àizǐ hěn qíguài, wèi shénme zhème kuài ne? Yuánlái, sījī bǎ tā sòngdàole dàxué de qiánménr.",en:`Very soon the driver told her, "Here's the front gate." Aiko was puzzled — why so fast? It turned out the driver had taken her to the university's front gate. (Qianmen is a famous place, but with the "-r" ending, 前门儿 just means "the front gate".)`}],vocab:[{w:"儿化音",py:"érhuàyīn",pos:"n.",en:"r-ending retroflexion"},{w:"闹笑话",py:"nào xiàohuà",pos:"v.",en:"make a fool of oneself"},{w:"门口",py:"ménkǒu",pos:"n.",en:"gate, doorway"},{w:"前门",py:"Qiánmén",pos:"n.",en:"Qianmen"},{w:"宿舍",py:"sùshè",pos:"n.",en:"dormitory"},{w:"出租车",py:"chūzūchē",pos:"n.",en:"taxi"},{w:"司机",py:"sījī",pos:"n.",en:"driver"},{w:"很快",py:"hěn kuài",pos:"adv.",en:"in a short time"}],points:[{name:"附近",en:"near, neighboring",eg:"那一天，爱子想去天安门附近的前门玩儿。",egEn:"That day, Aiko wanted to go and have fun at Qianmen, near Tian’anmen.",zh:"“附近”，名词，指离某个地方不远的地方，常说“……附近”，也可以放在名词前面，比如“附近的商店”。",enx:"“附近” is a noun meaning “nearby, the vicinity”. It is often used as “……附近” (near …), and can also go before a noun, e.g. “附近的商店” (nearby shops).",egs:["（1）我家附近有一个大超市。","（2）请问，这儿附近有银行吗？"]},{name:"这么",en:"so, such, like this",eg:"爱子很奇怪，为什么这么快呢？",egEn:"Aiko was puzzled — why so fast?",zh:"“这么”，代词，用在形容词或动词前面，表示程度很高，意思是“像这样”，常用来表示吃惊或感叹。",enx:"“这么” is a pronoun meaning “so, this (much)”. Placed before an adjective or a verb, it indicates a high degree and often expresses surprise.",egs:["（1）今天怎么这么冷？","（2）你的汉字写得这么好！"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"爱子不知道“前门”和“前门儿”的意思不一样。",a:!0},{q:"司机以为爱子要去大学的前门儿。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"她还很喜欢用儿化音，但是有一次闹了笑话。“闹了笑话”的意思是（ ）。",options:["开个玩笑","说个笑话","做了尴尬（embarrassing）的事情"],answer:2},{q:"爱子很奇怪，为什么这么快呢？“很奇怪”的意思是（ ）。",options:["很少见","觉得很不正常（weird）","很特别"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"天安门广场",titleEn:"Tian’anmen Square",zh:"天安门广场在北京市中心，是世界上最大的城市广场之一。广场北边是天安门，中间有人民英雄纪念碑，南边就是前门。1949年10月1日，中华人民共和国在这里举行了开国大典。今天，很多人一大早来这里看升国旗。",en:"Tian’anmen Square, in the centre of Beijing, is one of the largest city squares in the world. Tian’anmen (the Gate of Heavenly Peace) is on its north side, the Monument to the People’s Heroes stands in the middle, and Qianmen is at its south end. On October 1st, 1949, the founding ceremony of the People’s Republic of China was held here. Today, many people come here early in the morning to watch the national flag being raised."}},{n:22,title:"多变的气候",py:"Duōbiàn de qìhòu",en:"A Changeable Climate",chars:163,daodu:"冬天，北方人在看雪，南方人可能在海边游泳。中国的气候有什么有意思的地方？去吐鲁番旅行要带什么？",daoduEn:"In winter, while northerners are watching snow, southerners may be swimming at the beach. What’s interesting about China’s climate? And what should you take on a trip to Turpan?",paras:[{zh:"中国南方和北方的气候很不一样，特别是冬天，温度的差别很大。所以，北方人在看雪的时候，南方人可能在海边游泳。",py:"Zhōngguó nánfāng hé běifāng de qìhòu hěn bù yíyàng, tèbié shì dōngtiān, wēndù de chābié hěn dà. Suǒyǐ, běifāngrén zài kàn xuě de shíhou, nánfāngrén kěnéng zài hǎibiān yóuyǒng.",en:"The climates of southern and northern China are very different, especially in winter, when the temperature difference is huge. So while northerners are watching the snow, southerners may be swimming at the beach."},{zh:"在冬天，同一天的中午12点，哈尔滨的温度是－30℃，广州却可能是20℃，温度的差别有50℃。",py:"Zài dōngtiān, tóng yì tiān de zhōngwǔ 12 diǎn, Hā'ěrbīn de wēndù shì -30℃, Guǎngzhōu què kěnéng shì 20℃, wēndù de chābié yǒu 50℃.",en:"In winter, at 12 noon on the same day, it can be -30℃ in Harbin but 20℃ in Guangzhou — a difference of 50℃."},{zh:"有趣的是，在同一个地方，早晨和中午温度的差别也可能有30℃，夏天的吐鲁番就是这样的地方。",py:"Yǒuqù de shì, zài tóng yí gè dìfang, zǎochen hé zhōngwǔ wēndù de chābié yě kěnéng yǒu 30℃, xiàtiān de Tǔlǔfān jiù shì zhèyàng de dìfang.",en:"Interestingly, in one and the same place, the temperature can differ by 30℃ between morning and noon. Turpan in summer is such a place."},{zh:"那里的早晨特别冷，人们要穿很多衣服。中午又变得很热，要穿夏天的衣服。所以，如果你去吐鲁番旅行，一定要多带点儿衣服。",py:"Nàlǐ de zǎochen tèbié lěng, rénmen yào chuān hěn duō yīfu. Zhōngwǔ yòu biàn de hěn rè, yào chuān xiàtiān de yīfu. Suǒyǐ, rúguǒ nǐ qù Tǔlǔfān lǚxíng, yídìng yào duō dài diǎnr yīfu.",en:"Mornings there are very cold, and people have to wear lots of clothes. By noon it turns very hot, and you need summer clothes. So if you travel to Turpan, be sure to bring extra clothes."}],vocab:[{w:"南方",py:"nánfāng",pos:"n.",en:"south"},{w:"气候",py:"qìhòu",pos:"n.",en:"climate"},{w:"温度",py:"wēndù",pos:"n.",en:"temperature"},{w:"海边",py:"hǎibiān",pos:"n.",en:"beach"},{w:"同",py:"tóng",pos:"adj.",en:"same"},{w:"穿",py:"chuān",pos:"v.",en:"wear, put on"},{w:"有趣",py:"yǒuqù",pos:"adj.",en:"interesting"}],points:[{name:"差别",en:"difference",eg:"南方和北方的冬天，温度的差别很大。",egEn:"In winter, the temperature difference between the south and the north is huge.",zh:"“差别”，名词，指人或东西不一样的地方，常说“……的差别很大/很小”“A和B有差别”。",enx:"“差别” is a noun meaning “difference”. It is often used as “……的差别很大/很小” (the difference is big/small) or “A和B有差别” (A and B are different).",egs:["（1）这两件衣服的差别不大。","（2）北京和上海的天气差别很大。"]},{name:"旅行",en:"travel, take a trip",eg:"如果你去吐鲁番旅行，一定要多带点儿衣服。",egEn:"If you travel to Turpan, be sure to bring more clothes.",zh:"“旅行”，动词，意思是去比较远的地方游玩，常说“去……旅行”，后面一般不直接带宾语。",enx:"“旅行” is a verb meaning “to travel, to take a trip” to a faraway place. It is usually used as “去……旅行” and normally doesn’t take an object directly.",egs:["（1）放假以后，我想去云南旅行。","（2）他很喜欢一个人旅行。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"冬天，哈尔滨和广州的温差非常大。",a:!0},{q:"夏天的吐鲁番，早晨很热。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"冬天的时候，中国南方人可能去（ ）。",options:["看雪","游泳","滑雪"],answer:1},{q:"夏天在吐鲁番，早上要穿（ ）。",options:["很多衣服","夏天的衣服","春天的衣服"],answer:0}],tip:{title:"早穿皮袄午穿纱，晚抱火炉吃西瓜",titleEn:"Fur Jacket in the Morning, Gauze at Noon, Watermelon by the Stove at Night",zh:"这句俗语说的是新疆一些地方的天气，比如本课的吐鲁番。那里有很多沙漠，白天太阳出来以后温度上升得很快，晚上又下降得很快，所以一天里早晚很冷，中午很热：早上要穿皮袄，中午穿薄薄的纱衣，晚上一边烤火一边吃西瓜。",en:"This saying describes the weather in parts of Xinjiang, such as Turpan in this lesson. There are many deserts there: after the sun comes out, the temperature rises quickly, and at night it drops quickly again. So mornings and evenings are cold while noon is hot — you wear a fur jacket in the morning, thin gauze at noon, and in the evening you eat watermelon while warming yourself by the fire."}},{n:23,title:"长生果",py:"Chángshēngguǒ",en:"The Fruit of Eternal Life",chars:107,daodu:"听说吃了长生果就可以不死。有个人偷偷把皇帝的长生果吃了，皇帝非常生气。这个人会怎么样呢？",daoduEn:"It is said that if you eat the fruit of eternal life (长生果), you will never die. A man secretly ate the emperor’s fruit, and the emperor was furious. What will happen to him?",paras:[{zh:"中国古代，有人给皇帝送了一颗长生果，说吃了这颗长生果就可以不死。有个人知道后，偷偷把长生果吃了。",py:"Zhōngguó gǔdài, yǒu rén gěi huángdì sòngle yì kē chángshēngguǒ, shuō chīle zhè kē chángshēngguǒ jiù kěyǐ bù sǐ. Yǒu gè rén zhīdào hòu, tōutōu bǎ chángshēngguǒ chī le.",en:"In ancient China, someone gave the emperor a fruit of eternal life, saying that whoever ate it would never die. A man heard about it and secretly ate the fruit."},{zh:"皇帝非常生气，要杀死他。他一点儿也不害怕，对皇帝说：“如果长生果是真的，那我就不会死；如果我死了，那长生果一定不是真的。”皇帝觉得他很聪明，就没有杀他。",py:"Huángdì fēicháng shēngqì, yào shāsǐ tā. Tā yìdiǎnr yě bú hàipà, duì huángdì shuō: “Rúguǒ chángshēngguǒ shì zhēn de, nà wǒ jiù bú huì sǐ; rúguǒ wǒ sǐ le, nà chángshēngguǒ yídìng bú shì zhēn de.” Huángdì juéde tā hěn cōngming, jiù méiyǒu shā tā.",en:`The emperor was furious and wanted to kill him. The man wasn't afraid at all. He said to the emperor, "If the fruit of eternal life is real, then I can't die. If I die, then the fruit can't be real." The emperor thought he was very clever, so he didn't kill him.`}],vocab:[{w:"古代",py:"gǔdài",pos:"n.",en:"ancient times"},{w:"皇帝",py:"huángdì",pos:"n.",en:"emperor"},{w:"颗",py:"kē",pos:"m.",en:"measure word for small round things"},{w:"死",py:"sǐ",pos:"v.",en:"die"},{w:"杀",py:"shā",pos:"v.",en:"kill"},{w:"害怕",py:"hàipà",pos:"v.",en:"be afraid, be scared"},{w:"真",py:"zhēn",pos:"adj.",en:"real, genuine"}],points:[{name:"偷偷",en:"stealthily, covertly",eg:"有个人知道后，偷偷把长生果吃了。",egEn:"A man found out and secretly ate the fruit.",zh:"“偷偷”，副词，表示做事的时候不想让别人知道、看见，常说“偷偷（地）+动词”。",enx:"“偷偷” is an adverb meaning “secretly, stealthily” — doing something without letting others know or see. It is usually used as “偷偷（地）+ verb”.",egs:["（1）上课的时候，他偷偷看了一下手机。","（2）妹妹偷偷吃了我的蛋糕。"]},{name:"一点儿也不",en:"not at all, not a bit",eg:"他一点儿也不害怕。",egEn:"He wasn’t afraid at all.",zh:"“一点儿也不”放在形容词或动词前面，表示完全否定，语气很强，意思是“完全不”。也可以说“一点儿都不”。",enx:"“一点儿也不” goes before an adjective or a verb to express complete negation (“not at all”), with strong emphasis. “一点儿都不” is also used.",egs:["（1）这个菜一点儿也不辣。","（2）今天我一点儿也不累。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"吃了长生果可以不死。",a:!0},{q:"那个人是故意（intentionally）吃了长生果的。",a:!0},{q:"那个人觉得皇帝很聪明。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"那个人一点儿也不害怕，因为（ ）。",options:["他知道皇帝不会杀他","长生果是假的"],answer:0},{q:"皇帝后来没有杀他，因为（ ）。",options:["如果他死了，长生果就是假的","皇帝还有长生果"],answer:0}],tip:{title:"秦始皇",titleEn:"Emperor Qin Shi Huang",zh:"秦始皇（公元前259年—公元前210年）是中国历史上第一个皇帝。公元前221年，他统一了中国，建立了秦朝。他还统一了文字、钱和长度、重量的单位。秦始皇很想长生不老，派人到很多地方去找长生不老的药，可是他五十岁左右就死了。",en:"Qin Shi Huang (259–210 BC) was the first emperor in Chinese history. In 221 BC he unified China and founded the Qin Dynasty. He also standardized the writing system, the currency and the units of length and weight. Qin Shi Huang wanted very much to live forever and sent people to many places to look for an elixir of immortality, but he died at about fifty."}},{n:24,title:"我看见了大熊猫",py:"Wǒ kànjiànle dàxióngmāo",en:"I Saw Giant Pandas",chars:146,daodu:"“我”第一次参观北京动物园，看见了很多动物。“我”最喜欢哪种动物呢？",daoduEn:"The writer visits Beijing Zoo for the first time and sees lots of animals. Which animal does the writer like best?",paras:[{zh:"2010年8月8日 星期六 晴",py:"2010 nián 8 yuè 8 rì xīngqīliù qíng",en:"Saturday, August 8, 2010, sunny"},{zh:"今天我们和丁老师一起去北京动物园了，这是我来中国以后第一次参观动物园。我们是坐公共汽车去的，北京的车票特别便宜，只要四毛钱。",py:"Jīntiān wǒmen hé Dīng lǎoshī yìqǐ qù Běijīng Dòngwùyuán le, zhè shì wǒ lái Zhōngguó yǐhòu dì-yī cì cānguān dòngwùyuán. Wǒmen shì zuò gōnggòng qìchē qù de, Běijīng de chēpiào tèbié piányi, zhǐ yào sì máo qián.",en:"Today we went to the Beijing Zoo with Ms. Ding. It was my first visit to a zoo since coming to China. We went by bus. Bus tickets in Beijing are really cheap — only 40 fen (0.4 yuan)."},{zh:"北京动物园非常大，里面有很多动物。我最喜欢的当然是大熊猫了，今天我一次就看见了六只大熊猫，她们太可爱了！",py:"Běijīng Dòngwùyuán fēicháng dà, lǐmian yǒu hěn duō dòngwù. Wǒ zuì xǐhuan de dāngrán shì dàxióngmāo le, jīntiān wǒ yí cì jiù kànjiànle liù zhī dàxióngmāo, tāmen tài kě'ài le!",en:"The Beijing Zoo is very big, with lots of animals. My favorite, of course, is the giant panda. Today I saw six giant pandas all at once. They were so cute!"},{zh:"下个月我的男朋友来北京，他也很喜欢大熊猫，我还会和他一起再去参观北京动物园。",py:"Xià gè yuè wǒ de nánpéngyou lái Běijīng, tā yě hěn xǐhuan dàxióngmāo, wǒ hái huì hé tā yìqǐ zài qù cānguān Běijīng Dòngwùyuán.",en:"Next month my boyfriend is coming to Beijing. He loves giant pandas too, so I'll visit the Beijing Zoo again with him."}],vocab:[{w:"动物园",py:"dòngwùyuán",pos:"n.",en:"zoo"},{w:"参观",py:"cānguān",pos:"v.",en:"visit"},{w:"公共汽车",py:"gōnggòng qìchē",pos:"n.",en:"bus"},{w:"车票",py:"chēpiào",pos:"n.",en:"ticket"},{w:"当然",py:"dāngrán",pos:"adv.",en:"certainly"},{w:"可爱",py:"kě'ài",pos:"adj.",en:"lovely, cute"},{w:"男朋友",py:"nánpéngyou",pos:"n.",en:"boyfriend"}],points:[{name:"便宜",en:"cheap, low in price",eg:"北京的车票特别便宜，只要四毛钱。",egEn:"Bus tickets in Beijing are very cheap — only forty fen.",zh:"“便宜”，形容词，表示价钱低，和“贵”意思相反。",enx:"“便宜” is an adjective meaning “cheap, inexpensive”. Its opposite is “贵” (expensive).",egs:["（1）这家商店的东西又好又便宜。","（2）能便宜一点儿吗？"]},{name:"太……了",en:"so…, too…",eg:"今天我一次就看见了六只大熊猫，她们太可爱了！",egEn:"Today I saw six giant pandas all at once — they were so cute!",zh:"“太……了”，中间放形容词或表示心理的动词，表示程度很高，常用来感叹；有时也表示“过分”，比如“太贵了”。",enx:"In “太……了”, an adjective or a verb of feeling goes in the middle. It expresses a high degree, often as an exclamation; it can also mean “too (much)”, e.g. “太贵了” (too expensive).",egs:["（1）你来了，太好了！","（2）这件衣服太大了，我不能穿。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"今天是我来中国以后第一次看见大熊猫。",a:!0},{q:"北京的公共汽车票很便宜。",a:!0},{q:"我的男朋友这个月来北京。",a:!1}],mc:[{q:"我太喜欢大熊猫了，下个月我还要（ ）动物园。",options:["参观","学习"],answer:0},{q:"动物园的门票淡季（dànjì，off-season）特别（ ），一张10元。",options:["贵","便宜"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"北京动物园",titleEn:"Beijing Zoo",zh:"北京动物园在北京城的西边，是中国开放最早的动物园之一，到现在已经有一百多年的历史了。动物园很大，里面有很多种动物，最受欢迎的是大熊猫。大熊猫是中国特有的动物，非常可爱，很多人来北京旅游，都要去动物园看看它们。",en:"Beijing Zoo, in the west of the city, is one of the earliest zoos opened in China and has a history of more than a hundred years. The zoo is very big and has many kinds of animals; the most popular are the giant pandas. Giant pandas are found only in China and are very cute, so many people who visit Beijing go to the zoo to see them."}},{n:25,title:"我开博客了",py:"Wǒ kāi bókè le",en:"I've Started a Blog",chars:126,daodu:"高希希来中国已经半年了，去了很多地方。朋友们都想看看高希希眼里的中国，有什么好办法呢？",daoduEn:"Gao Xixi has been in China for half a year and has been to lots of places. Friends all want to see China through Gao Xixi’s eyes. Is there a good way to do that?",paras:[{zh:"我叫高希希，来中国已经半年了，去了很多地方旅游。",py:"Wǒ jiào Gāo Xīxī, lái Zhōngguó yǐjīng bàn nián le, qùle hěn duō dìfang lǚyóu.",en:"My name is Gao Xixi. I've been in China for half a year now and have traveled to many places."},{zh:"朋友们知道后，都很羡慕，希望我发一些照片给他们。有朋友说：“你开一个博客（blog）吧，把你看到的中国拍出来，让我们也看一看。”",py:"Péngyoumen zhīdào hòu, dōu hěn xiànmù, xīwàng wǒ fā yìxiē zhàopiàn gěi tāmen. Yǒu péngyou shuō: “Nǐ kāi yí gè bókè (blog) ba, bǎ nǐ kàndào de Zhōngguó pāi chūlai, ràng wǒmen yě kàn yi kàn.”",en:`When my friends found out, they were all envious and wanted me to send them some photos. One friend said, "Why don't you start a blog? Take photos of the China you see, so we can have a look too."`},{zh:"我觉得这是一个好主意，所以今天我开博客了（http://blog.sina.com.cn/zhubrook），欢迎你们！",py:"Wǒ juéde zhè shì yí gè hǎo zhǔyi, suǒyǐ jīntiān wǒ kāi bókè le (http://blog.sina.com.cn/zhubrook), huānyíng nǐmen!",en:"I thought this was a good idea, so today I started a blog (http://blog.sina.com.cn/zhubrook). Welcome, everyone!"},{zh:"昨天我去了中国最有名的大学——北京大学，所以我的第一篇博客就是“美丽的北大”。",py:"Zuótiān wǒ qùle Zhōngguó zuì yǒumíng de dàxué — Běijīng Dàxué, suǒyǐ wǒ de dì-yī piān bókè jiù shì “Měilì de Běidà”.",en:'Yesterday I went to the most famous university in China — Peking University. So my first blog post is called "Beautiful Peking University".'}],vocab:[{w:"半年",py:"bànnián",pos:"n.",en:"half a year"},{w:"发",py:"fā",pos:"v.",en:"send"},{w:"让",py:"ràng",pos:"v.",en:"let"},{w:"有名",py:"yǒumíng",pos:"adj.",en:"well-known"},{w:"篇",py:"piān",pos:"m.",en:"measure word for written work"},{w:"美丽",py:"měilì",pos:"adj.",en:"beautiful"}],points:[{name:"羡慕",en:"envy",eg:"朋友们知道后，都很羡慕。",egEn:"When my friends found out, they were all envious.",zh:"“羡慕”，动词，表示看到别人有好的东西或好的条件，自己也很希望有，常说“很羡慕”“羡慕+人”。",enx:"“羡慕” is a verb meaning “to envy, to admire”: seeing that others have something good, you wish you had it too. It is often used as “很羡慕” or “羡慕 + someone”.",egs:["（1）他的汉语说得那么好，我很羡慕他。","（2）大家都羡慕她有一个好工作。"]},{name:"V.+出来",en:"verb + 出来 (bring out, make visible)",eg:"你开一个博客吧，把你看到的中国拍出来。",egEn:"Why don’t you start a blog and take pictures of the China you see?",zh:"“V.+出来”中，“出来”放在动词后面，表示通过这个动作，让东西从没有到有、从看不见到看得见，比如“拍出来”“写出来”“想出来”。",enx:"In “V.+出来”, “出来” after a verb shows that, through the action, something comes into being or becomes visible, e.g. “拍出来” (capture in photos), “写出来” (write out), “想出来” (think up).",egs:["（1）这个问题很难，我想不出来。","（2）请你把你的想法写出来。"]}],think:[],tf:[{q:"高希希来中国已经6个月了。",a:!0},{q:"高希希很喜欢在中国旅游。",a:!0},{q:"高希希昨天去了北京大学。",a:!0}],mc:[{q:"他家的孩子考上了北京大学，真让人（ ）。",options:["羡慕","奇怪"],answer:0},{q:"朋友建议（jiànyì，advise）我去西藏，我觉得这是个不错的（ ）。",options:["意见","主意"],answer:1}],tip:{title:"博客",titleEn:"Blog",zh:"“博客”是英语“blog”的音译，写博客的人叫“博主”。人们可以在博客上写文章、发照片，和朋友分享自己的生活，别人也可以在下面留言。博客21世纪初进入中国以后，很快就流行起来了，新浪博客、搜狐博客等都很有名。本课的高希希用的就是新浪博客。",en:"“博客” is a transliteration of the English word “blog”, and a person who writes a blog is called a “博主” (blogger). On a blog, people can write articles and post photos to share their lives with friends, and others can leave comments. After blogs came to China in the early 2000s, they quickly became popular; Sina Blog and Sohu Blog were both well known. Gao Xixi in this lesson uses Sina Blog."}}],h={key:e,title:n,titleEn:a,series:i,seriesEn:o,level:t,lessons:s};export{h as default,e as key,s as lessons,t as level,i as series,o as seriesEn,n as title,a as titleEn};
